{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"wc -l PLAN.md TASK.md; rg -n '\"'^## |''^### '\"' PLAN.md; ls -la\"","aggregated_output":"  1099 PLAN.md\n   151 TASK.md\n  1250 total\n15:## 1. The game in one page\n58:## 2. Originality\n68:## 3. World and story\n70:### The world\n80:### The cast\n95:### The story\n120:### Writing style\n137:## 4. Combat\n139:### Controls\n162:### Aiming\n168:### Feel numbers (starting values, all sliders in section 15)\n175:### The strike recipe (pillar 1)\n195:### Streaks\n200:### Life and death\n209:## 5. Heroes\n220:### Bram Tolliver, the Ringer: melee bruiser\n238:### Brother Iven, the Cantor: ranged caster\n256:### Wren Ashby, the Lamplighter: ranged skirmisher\n274:### Maud Harrow, the Sexton: summoner\n296:## 6. Monsters and bosses\n325:### Elites\n345:### Bosses\n372:## 7. Loot and progression\n374:### Items\n412:### Town services\n422:### Numbers (starting values; tune with the sliders and the bot)\n447:## 8. Zones and features\n468:### The Long Vigil\n476:### Events and small things\n487:### The feature tour\n519:## 9. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n521:### Rules\n530:### Settings additions\n542:### Screens (all canvas, one panel kit, section 17)\n568:### Touch-only devices ✔\n578:## 10. Art direction\n606:## 11. Animation\n627:## 12. Audio: all in code, no files\n665:## 13. Multiplayer\n671:### World code shared by all modes\n674:### Couch co-op\n677:### AI Hub session: the round\n701:### Network design (`authority` on the host, puppets elsewhere)\n718:### Tests\n723:## 14. Attract mode\n746:## 15. Dev mode and designer tools\n748:### Dev Mode (pause menu item, hidden in sessions)\n766:### The Gallery (from Dev Mode, deep link `#gallery`)\n769:### So the rest could be built with designer tools\n779:## 16. Deliverables, About/Credits and the paperwork\n781:### What you hand over\n801:### Source Information\n821:### Feedback questions\n844:### About/Credits screen\n847:### Exit interview\n877:## 17. Tech plan\n879:### Working environment\n887:### Setup\n898:### Files\n912:### Architecture rules (these prevent the expensive rewrites)\n936:### Game creation (the parts verified or that trap people)\n945:### The parts bin: Emberdeep\n963:### Engine changes to expect (you may change anything; keep a list for the feedback)\n967:### Traps\n978:## 18. Testing\n1011:## 19. Order of work and cut order\n1031:### Cut order\n1049:## 20. Coverage checklist (TASK.md to this plan)\ntotal 132\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha   4096 Nov  5 10:34 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha   4096 Nov  5 10:34 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 107791 Nov  5 10:34 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  12494 Nov  5 10:34 TASK.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
