{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '155,245p' API.md; cat docs/ASSETS.md\"","aggregated_output":"- `r.w(x, y, z)` = buffer pixel of a world point. `r.W`, `r.H`, `r.ix`, `r.iy` (pass to dither functions), `r.view`, `r.visible(x, y, z)`.\n- X-ray: `r.actor(..., { xray: true })` shows the actor's hidden part, a translucent tint with a 1-px outline (a checker in `E.style.trans = 'dither'`), wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high (22; `hides: true | false` says otherwise) or anything queued with `{ hides: true }` is drawn in front of it; not by one rising less than 8 above its feet (the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall). `xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors: true }`: with `actors` other bodies in front hide it too (a hero stays findable in a crowd). Afterimages: `ghost: { color, life, alpha, owner }`; `owner` (the actor's `{x, y, z}`) keeps a trail left nearer the camera sorted behind the live body.\n- Glowing things you draw yourself: `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, { emissive: true })` is drawn again after lighting so darkness never dims it (flames, lasers, magic, neon). It still hides behind whatever stands in front of it: walls and `r.actor` bodies do this on their own, and any other queued draw can join them with `{ solid: true }`. (Canvas lighting builds a depth-ordered mask for this; `game.r.glowMask = false` skips it on slow machines.)\n\n## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`, `dot`, `line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, width)`, `disc(g, x, y, r, c)`, `ell`, `poly(g, pts, c)`, `polyDither(g, pts, c, 0..1, r.ix, r.iy)`, `ddisc`, `sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip)` (or `{ flip, rot, scale }`), `glow(g, 0..1)` (GPU glow for what follows).\n- Sprites from strings (for coins, bullets, ships, icons, NES-style enemies): `const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }, scale)`. `.` and space are transparent. Frames: `const walk = E.anim([f1, f2, f3], 8, { pingpong })` (or one sheet: `E.anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 })`), drawn with `r.sprite(x, y, z, walk, { t })`. `r.sprite(..., { rot: angle, scale })` turns and scales in whole pixels (cached in 16 steps a turn; `steps: 32`); `E.recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a' })` swaps a palette.\n- Font (5x7 proportional with lower case: ASCII, the face buttons, arrows, ★ ♥ ♪ ✓ … ° € £, the accented Latin letters; any other is `?`; `font: 'tiny'` for 3x5): `E.font.text(g, str, x, y, color, { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font })`, `E.font.title(g, str, x, y, { scale, colors, outline, depth, depthColor, align })`, `E.font.width(str, opts)`, `E.font.lineHeight(opts)`, `E.font.wrap(str, maxW, opts)`. Glyphs: ASCII plus `♥ ★ ← → ↑ ↓ • × ♪ ▸ ©`.\n- UI (inside `r.overlay(g => ...)`): `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, gradient, alpha })` (a gradient window like Final Fantasy; `bg` can be `[top, bottom]`, `gradient: false` for flat, `alpha: .6` for a see-through HUD panel), `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, color)`, `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max)` (half hearts allowed), `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg, frame, cape: false, weapon: false, tint: '#808080' })` (character close-up; it stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down; `tint` greys out a KO'd hero).\n- Dialog: `const talk = new E.Dialog(game)`; `talk.say(['Line one.', 'Page two.'], { name: 'ELDER', portrait: elderRig, onDone, choices: ['YES', 'NO'], onChoice(i) })` (choices show on the last page: the keys, or a tap or click on one, pick); in update `if (talk.update(dt)) return;` (true while a modal box is open: play waits); in draw `talk.draw(r)`. `portrait` takes a Humanoid (live close-up; `portraitSize: 40`, `portraitOpts: { zoom, turn }`) or a function `(g, x, y, size) => {...}`. Radio chatter during play: `talk.say('Enemy fighters ahead!', { name, portrait, auto: 2.5, modal: false })` turns its pages and closes by itself while the game keeps running. Per line: `place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom'`, `y` (pixels) and `alpha` (see-through box). `new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars })` (`voice`: a sound, or `(ch, i, talk) => {}` per letter); `talk.close()`, `talk.open`. Markup in the text: `{c=#ffd36a}gold{/c}` a color, `{w=.5}` a pause, `{s=12}slowly{/s}` letters a second, `{shake}..{/shake}`, `{wave}..{/wave}`, `{$name}` a value from `say(text, { vars })` or `talk.vars`.\n- Menu: `const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', { label: 'LOAD', disabled: true }], { x: 'center', y: 100, title, onPick(i, item), onCancel, scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (rows: it scrolls); `menu.update(dt)`; `menu.draw(r)`. Keys, d-pad and sticks move it; a click or tap on an entry picks it (so a phone can leave a title), and the mouse over one moves the cursor. A tap on a dialog box turns its page as confirm does.\n- HTML screens and HUD: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { scale: 2 } (a TV; or `tv: true`), settings, screens: { pause, help, dev: { rows: ['glyphs'] } } })`; `ui.show('title' | 'results' | 'map' | ..., spec)`; each step `ui.hud({ objective, status, bars, prompt, minimap })` (`minimap: { map, fog, camera: true, markers, onClick(x, y) }`); `ui.toast(title, text)`.\n\n## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\n- `sfx(name, { vol, pitch, pan, loop })` → `{ stop(), set({ pan, vol }) }` (a loop sounds on: an engine, rain). Presets: `jump jump2 land step coin pickup key powerup oneup heal hit hurt stomp bump swing whoosh punch kick shoot laser charge explode boom door secret warp die select confirm cancel pause text blip`.\n- Custom: `sfx({ wave: 'square' | 'pulse' | 'pulse12' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'sine' | 'noise', freq: 440 or 'A4', to: 880, dur: .2, vol: .3, arp: [0, 4, 7], step: .05, vib: [8, .03] })`, or `audio.define('zap', voice)`; `audio.instrument('pluck', (ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) => ...)` is a `wave` too.\n- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 . . . | ...' }, { wave: 'triangle', notes: '...' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] }`. Tokens: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holds, `.` rests, `|` is ignored; drums `k s h o c t`. `music(null)` stops. `mute()`, `setVolume(0..1)` (or set `audio.musicVolume`, `sfxVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), `duck(on)` (quieter music under your own pause or map screen). Your own Web Audio connects to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, under the volume and mute.\n- The music clock (the full engine): a song's place is game time, headless too, and the sound follows it. `music(song, { sync: true })` pauses with the game (else it plays on); `audio.pos` → `{ t, step, beat, bar, at, loop, bpm, layers, playing }`; `at(step, fn)`, `onBeat(fn)` (on the update step); `tempo(bpm)`; `layer(name or index, vol, fade)` (a track's `name`, `on: false` starts it silent: the chase's drums in by layers); `music(song, { fade: 1 })` crossfades; `sting(song, { at: 'bar' })` over the music; `sfx(voice, { step })` on a step of the music. `settings.audioOffset` (ms, Settings, Sound: Calibrate) sets `audio.offset`; `audio.calibrate()` → `{ tap(), result, done, stop() }`.\n\n## Levels\n**TileMap** (top-down, isometric, brawler): walls stand on the ground plane.\n- `new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorTex, block: ['water', 'lava'], ao: 5, outside })` (`ao` = width of the contact shadow along wall bases, 0 = none; `outside`: the ground past the map, a color, or `false` for none). `types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut: true, cutH, face, roof, beam }` (`cut` lowers walls that block the camera, those `map.isFront(cx, cy, view)` says; a map may replace it; `face`: `'brick'` (default) `'stone' 'rock' 'plank' 'timber' 'plaster' 'hedge' 'none'`; `roof`: `'speckle'` (default) `'plain' 'tiles' 'slab' 'leaves' 'grass'`; `beam` = timber color). `floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view)` returns `[r, g, b]` (or `[r, g, b, glow]`); ready-made: `E.tex.flagstone`, `grass`, `dirt`, `water`, `planks`, `checker`, `plain`. A map of more than 128 x 128 cells bakes its floor in squares as the camera comes to them and lets the far ones go (`chunks: true | false` to choose; `map.floorBytes()` what it holds), so a 256 x 256 world map costs what the screen shows.\n- Legend values: a number = wall type, a string = spawn tag, `{ tile, floor, spawn, block }` for both. `block: true` (or the map's `block` list of floor tags) makes deep water, lava or pits stop walkers (jumping bodies pass over); `walkable(cx, cy)`, `block(cx, cy, on)` (a bridge appears). FlowField paths go around blocked cells and follow `block` and `set` at their next `update`.\n- `find(tag)` / `findAll(tag)` give `{ x, y, z, cx, cy }`. Also `cell(cx, cy)`, `set(cx, cy, id)` (open doors), `toCell(x, y)`, `center(cx, cy)`, `heightAt(x, y)`, `floorAt(x, y)`, `groundAt(x, y, r, z)`, `collide(body)`, `los(x0, y0, x1, y1)` (ground only), `bounds(view)` (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }`, buffer pixels), `drawFloor(r)`, `queueWalls(r)`.\n\n**Heights** (collision, standing, sight, reach and navigation share one rule): a body's `z` is its feet; a cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)` (0 = floor); a body stands on the highest top within `z + 2`. Eyes at `z + E.HEIGHTS.eye` (30) see a target at `z + E.HEIGHTS.chest` (22); a body's own `eye` / `chest` override them (crouching). Same level: `|dz| <= 8`. On a TileMap (`dir` = an angle or `[dx, dy]`): `ray(a, b, { eye, target })` → `{ clear, t, x, y, z }`, `sight(a, b)`, `standable(x, y, z, r)`, `ledge(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, rise, facing, edge }` (climb), `landing(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, d }` (a jump across a gap), `drop(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, fall }`, `arcClear(a, b, apex, r)`, `pick(sx, sy)` → `{ cx, cy, z, face }` (the cell under a screen point: `input.clicked()`, any view and turn). Helpers: `E.sameLevel(a, b)`, `E.targets(from, list, { range, arc, dz, sight: map })` → `[{ target, d, dz, angle }]` nearest first, `E.inArc(..., dz)`. `new E.FlowField(map, { climb, drop, jump })` paths over roofs, between levels and across gaps.\n\n**PlatformMap** (side-scrollers; 2.5D in tilted views): tiles on the x/z plane, top row first.\n- `new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types })`. `types[id] = { kind, style, side, top, line, mat }` (`mat`: any material for a solid tile's face). Example: `rows: ['      ?    ', '   ===     ', '@  g   ^^  ', '###########']`, `legend: { '#': 1, '=': 2, '?': 3, '^': 4, '@': 'hero', 'g': 'walker' }`, `types: { 1: { style: 'ground', side: '#8a5a32' }, 2: { kind: 'oneway' }, 3: { style: 'bonus', side: '#e8a830' }, 4: { kind: 'hazard' } }`. Kinds: `'solid'` (default), `'oneway'` (jump up through), `'ladder'`, `'slope'` (`dir: 1` rises to the right, `-1` to the left; `from` / `to` heights 0..1 for gentle slopes), `'hazard'` (spikes, lava), `'deco'`, `'back'` (background wall). Styles: `'stone'` (`moss`) `'brick' 'wood' 'metal' 'ground'` (`flower`) `'block' 'pipe' 'bonus' 'plank' 'spikes' 'ladder' 'liquid' 'plain'`.\n- Spawns: `find(tag)` gives `{ x, z }` with z = the bottom of that cell (feet). Standing on the ground means z = the top of the floor tiles (`level.groundBelow(x, z)`, which returns `null` over a pit), not z = 0. `cell(cx, cz)` / `set(cx, cz, id)` count cz from the bottom row. `slopeZ(cx, cz, x)`, `touching(body, 'hazard')`, `cellsTouching(body, kind)`, `groundBelow(x, z)`, `solidAt(x, z)`, `move(body, dt, solids)`, `bounds(view)`, `draw(r)` (call first, after `r.sky`), `width`, `height`.\n\n## Movement and physics\n**Platformer** (side-scroller character): `const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22, run: 95, jump: 285, gravity: 800, airJumps: 0, wallJump: false, dash: 0 })`.\n- Each update: `hero.update(dt, level, game.input, movingPlatforms)`. For enemies pass `{ x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash }` instead of the input.\n- Read: `onGround`, `jumped`, `landed`, `facing` (1 or -1), `air`, `climbing`, `hitWall`, `hitCeiling`, `bumped` (`{ cx, cz, id }` of a block hit from below). Methods: `knock(dir)`, `rigState(extra)` (feed it to `rig.update`).\n- Built in: coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height (let go early for a short hop), slopes and small steps (sticks to the ground going down), ladders (up / down), drop through one-way tiles (down + jump), optional double jump, wall jump and dash.\n- Further moves, each on request: `crouch` (down: half as tall, it crawls), `ledge` (catches a ledge falling past it; up climbs), `wallCling`, `momentum` (slopes, a roll, a charged dash); tile kinds `'water'` (it swims), `'rope'` (up grabs it), `'bars'` (it hangs and travels), grip `friction` (ice .15), `carry` (a conveyor), `bounce` (a spring), `crumble` and `respawn` (`level.update(dt)` each step); `hero.swingFrom(x, z)` (a grapple: a pendulum, jump lets go); draw `level.drawWater(r)` after the actors. State: `crouching`, `hanging`, `clinging`, `swimming`, `onRope`, `onBars`, `swinging`, `rolling`; `rigState()` poses them.\n- Moving platforms: `{ x, z, w, h, vx, vz }` boxes you move yourself and pass as `solids`; riders are carried.\n\n**Body** (top-down / isometric / brawler): `new E.Body({ x, y, r: 5, friction: 0, bounce: 0, gravity: 700 })`. Set `vx`, `vy`, then `body.update(dt, map)`. Also `push(ix, iy, iz)` (knockback), `jump(v)`, and `onGround`, `z`, `groundZ`, `hitWall`, `landed`, `bounced` (hit the ground and bounced: dust, a thud). Walls lower than your feet are walkable, so bodies can jump onto blocks.\n\n**Mover** (third person): `const mover = new E.Mover({ x, y })`; `mover.update(dt, map, game.input)` (input `'THIRDPERSON'`) or an AI's `{ move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }`: it sprints, sneaks, climbs, vaults, leaps gaps, hops down and rolls; `climbAny: true` climbs any wall (jump at it; up the screen is up the wall; jump leaps up, crouch lets go; `mover.wall`, `map.wall(from, dir)`), `glide: true` glides (jump again in the air; `lift`: an updraft), `staminaMax: 100` (climbing, gliding and sprinting spend `mover.stamina`); `rig.update(dt, mover.rigState())`; `mover.play('takedown', { other })`, your own `E.ACTIONS`. Stealth: `E.sees(guard, hero, { map })` → `{ seen, exposure }`, `E.hears`, `new E.Suspicion()` (`update(dt, seen, hero)` → `'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'`), `r.sightCone(guard, { map })`, `r.marker(x, y, z, { label })`.\n\n**Attack** (melee timing for swords, punches, kicks): `const slash = new E.Attack('slash')` (a move from `E.MOVES`, optionally with overrides: `new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 })`) or a spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, wind, active, recover }`. `if (input.buffered('attack') && slash.start()) input.consume('attack')`; `slash.update(dt)` (returns the phase that just began); `slash.hits(enemies, e => E.inArc(hero, facing, e, 22, 1.4), e => {...})` hits each target once per swing during `'active'` (moves wait until `hitAt: .35` of the swing, so hit-stop freezes the strike, not the wind-up); `rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: slash.state })`. Also `busy`, `active`, `cancel()`. **Combo**: `const combo = new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut'], { window: .3 })` (names, specs or Attacks); `combo.press()` starts or chains the next hit; `update`, `hits`, `state`, `step` work the same. **Knockback**: `E.knockback(attacker, target, 160, up)` pushes a Body (or anything with vx / vy) away.\n\n**Bullets**: `const shots = new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side' })`; `shots.fire({ x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r: 2, team: 'player', color, life, dmg, pierce, sprite })`; `shots.burst(base, E.pattern.spread(angle, n, arc, speed))`; `shots.update(dt, map)`; `shots.hit(targets, (b, t) => {...}, 'player')`; `shots.draw(r)`; `shots.clear(team)`. Patterns: `E.pattern.dir(angle, speed)`, `aim(a, b, speed)`, `aimSide(a, b, speed)`, `spread(angle, n, arc, speed)`, `ring(n, speed, offset)`. In side view the second number of a pattern velocity is vz.\n\n**Helpers**: `E.dist(a, b)`, `E.angleTo(a, b)`, `E.arc(a, b, gravity, { apex | time | speed })` → `{ vx, vy, vz, t }` (a throw that lands at b: a lob, a grenade), `E.overlap(a, b)` (circles x, y, r), `E.overlapBox(a, b)` (side boxes x center, z feet, w, h), `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)` (melee cone; `dz` limits the height difference), `E.rand(a, b)`, `E.randInt(a, b)`, `E.pick(list)`, `E.chance(p)`, `E.prune(list, fn)`, `E.store.get(key, fallback)` / `set(key, value)` (save data; slots: `game.saves`), `new E.SpatialHash(32)` (`build(list)`, `near(x, y, r, fn)`), `new E.FlowField(map)` (`update(tx, ty)` or `update([[x, y], ...])`: the nearest; `dir(x, y, tx, ty)` walks around walls and `map.solid` shapes), math `clamp lerp approach ease.* angDiff approachAng smoothDamp rng(seed) noise2 hex shade mix`; `E.version` (the release) and `E.versionLabel()` ('v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': show it on a title or a debug screen).\n\n## Characters\n**Humanoid** (knights, heroes, soldiers, zombies): `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'chibi' (default) | 'heroic' (tall) | 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) | 'skeleton' (tint with colors.bone), weapon: 'sword' (the default) | 'gun' | 'staff' | null (fists) | a game's own (`E.Humanoid.weapon(id, { length, rest, draw(w) })`; `.hat(id, draw)`, `.pose(id, (J, w) => ...)`; `draw: { under, over }`; state `tilt`, `roll`), outfit: 'shirt' | 'tunic' | 'robe' | 'coat', hair: 'short' | 'spiky' | 'long' | 'ponytail' | 'bald', hat: 'cap' | 'pointed' | 'helmet' | 'band' | 'crown' (or { style, color }), sleeves: 'short' | 'long' | 'none', armor, hood (in colors.hair), cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.5 }, eyeGlow, hunch, lean, style: 'hd' (default) | 'classic' (stick figures for huge crowds), colors: { skin, hair, cloth, coat, pants, boot, belt, trim, glove, cape, capeIn, metal, plate, hilt, eye, iris } })` (`metal` colors the weapon, `plate` the armor, defaulting to `metal`).\n- `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, air, point, aim, attack })`. `facing` is an angle (side view: 0 = right, `Math.PI` = left). `air: true` tucks the legs for jumps; `point: true` holds a gun forward; `aim` tilts it (radians, + = up: `aim: .8` shoots diagonally up, `Math.PI / 2` straight up).\n- **Moves** (`E.MOVES`, use them instead of hand-made specs; every one has anticipation, a committed strike with lunge / step / lean / twist, follow-through and a clean return to the stance, on every build and in every view):\n  - blades and clubs: `slash backslash overhead rising thrust spin plunge twohand`;\n  - fists: `jab` (left hand) `cross hook uppercut haymaker elbow`;\n  - kicks: `kick roundhouse sweep flyingkick knee axekick`;\n  - other: `cast` (both hands) `throw bash claw`.\n  Give each character its own set (a knight: `overhead`, `thrust`, `spin`; a mage: `cast`; a monk: `jab`, `cross`, `roundhouse`; a boss: `haymaker`, `sweep`). `E.move('uppercut', .5)` is the attack state of any move at any moment (previews, cutscenes).\n- `attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }`, spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, r0, r1, hand, rel, blade, spin, kick, plane, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`. Angles are relative to facing (+ = right hand side). `rel: true`: heights relative to the shoulder and reach scaled by arm length (kick heights as a share of hip height). `r0`/`r1`: reach that extends (thrusts, jabs). `hand: 'L' | 'both'`. In side views horizontal swings turn into the screen plane (a Castlevania chop) by themselves; `plane: 'side' | 'ground'` (or the rig option `swingPlane`) chooses. `lunge` steps into the strike (body motion in local units, clamped to -4..5; to move the character itself, add speed to your body), `hop` lifts the body, `crouch` dips in the wind-up, `hold` is how long the end pose holds (share of recover). You time the phases.\n- In steep ground views (threequarter) rigs and Blobs are drawn from a lower, sprite-like angle so faces show, like SNES RPG sprites (`charView: false` turns it off for one rig, `E.style.charPitch = false` for all).\n- Faces (eyes with catch-lights, brows, mouth), a cheated 3/4 turn toward the camera in side views (`cheat: .5`, 0 turns it off) and hair layers are automatic. `face: { eyes: 'big' (anime / Mana style), bangs: 0..1 }`.\n- Poses: `rig.update(dt, { ..., pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' })` (they blend in and out), `'block'` (weapon upright across the body), `'die'` (a stagger, then the body topples), `expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince'` (faces and portraits), `run: 0..1` (run in place), or `down: 0..1` to lie a defeated body flat. `stance: 'guard'` keeps fists up while walking (brawlers; the free hand guards the chin during punches), `stance: 'ready'` holds the weapon forward. `climb: true` with `vz` climbs a ladder hand over hand (`Platformer.rigState()` passes both). Traversal: `crouch` (a sneaking gait), `sprint` (a lean), `hang` with `hangZ` (hands on an edge that high above the feet), `flip: 0..1` (a roll), `land: k` (a heavy landing); `mover.rigState()` sets them. Every wind-up starts from the rig's current pose, so chained hits and hand changes never snap. Idle rigs breathe and shift their weight by themselves.\n- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)` inside `r.actor`, `rig.drawSmear(r)` (a glowing trail along the real blade, fist or foot path, in every view), `rig.debug(r)` (skeleton), `rig.kick(v)` (squash and stretch), `rig.hand()` and `rig.tip()` (world points to spawn bullets from), `rig.worldOffset(p)` (where a point in the rig's own frame, such as a joint in `rig.J`, sits from its feet: to draw or spawn at any joint), `rig.lastView` (the view it last drew with), `rig.solvePose()` (sets `rig.J` from its state each step: wrap it on one rig to move joints).\n**Blob** (slimes, rabbites, bats, imps, round monsters): `new E.Blob({ R: 6, colors: { dk, base, lt, spec, eye, pupil }, ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true, feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true | 'fangs', face: 'front' })`, `update(dt, { squash: -0.4..0.4, look: [dx, dy], squint, walk: 0..1, flap: 0..1 (wing speed; 0 folds them), hang: true (roost upside down) })`, `kick(v)`, `draw(g, ox, oy, view)`. Mix the parts for a bestiary: `wings` + `mouth: 'fangs'` is a bat, `ears: 'rabbit'` + `feet` a Mana rabbite, `horns` + `tail` an imp.\n\n## Effects and lighting\n- Particles: `game.particles.explosion(x, y, z, size)` (fireball, smoke, sparks, debris, ring, shake, sound), `fire(x, y, z, n, { size })`, `smoke(x, y, z, n, { size, color })`, `glints(x, y, z, n, color)`, `dust(x, y, z, n)`, `sparks(x, y, z, n, angle)`, `bits(x, y, z, n, colors)`, `ring(x, y, r0, r1, color, dur)`, `text(x, y, z, '12', color, { scale: 2, bounce: true })` (bouncing damage numbers), `add({ kind: 'dust' | 'spark' | 'bit' | 'ember' | 'fire' | 'smoke' | 'glint', ... })`. `explosion(x, y, z, size, { debris, freeze: false, shake: 0 })` for chains of small blasts. Side-scrollers: `particles.ground = (x, y, z) => level.groundBelow(x, z)` so sparks and debris bounce on platforms. Screen flash: `game.flash('#ffffff', .12, strength 0..1)`.\n- Lighting (step 9; every view, side-scrollers included, no WebGPU needed): `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity, { color: '#ffa050' })` every draw. Dark areas get a smooth cool tint, lights add their own color, and emissive items (flames, sparks, bullets, `emissive: true`) stay bright. `lights.darkness` (0..1) and `lights.tint` tune it; after setting `lights.dark = [r, g, b]`, `levels` or `glow`, call `lights.refresh()`. Props with flames can light the scene: `r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { light: true })`. Lamps, street lamps, lanterns and crystals glow on their own (`haloR`, `haloColor`, `halo: false`); `cone: true` adds a light cone under a street lamp.\n- Hits: `game.hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage: 12, textScale: 2, textZ: 22 })` does hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks, a bouncing damage number (`bounce: false` floats it) and a sound in one call; `particles.impact(x, y, z, size, color)` for the star alone.\n- GPU lighting (optional, ground views with a TileMap): `const gpu = game.enableGPU({ map })`; mark glowing things with `px.glow(g, 1)`; add `lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` and `lights.heat(x, y, z, w)`. Where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with `game.lights.ambient` (`gpu.fallback = false`: unlit).\n\n## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n| Genre (examples) | View | Build it with | Copy slice |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Platformer (Mario, Mega Man, Sonic, Castlevania) | `side` (+ `brawler` for 2.5D) | PlatformMap, Platformer, Humanoid, sprites, Bullets `'side'` | PLATFORMER |\n| Metroidvania (Metroid, Symphony of the Night) | `side` | an `E.World` of PlatformMaps (the rooms module: doors at open edges, a slide, the explored map, gates opened by abilities, saves), a Platformer given `airJumps` and `dash` as they are found, its further moves, an arm cannon aimed eight ways (`point`, `aim`, `rig.tip()`, Bullets) | METROIDVANIA |\n| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\n| Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword) | none: rooms painted in screen pixels (`r.overlay`) | `E.Click` (the click module): rooms with walk areas and holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots, the nine verbs, Sierra's icons or a verb coin, an inventory, puzzles as rules; talk through `E.Story` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad) | none | `E.Story` nodes and choices over a painted backdrop, `rig.drawPortrait` at size, `story.log` (the backlog), `story.auto`, `story.skip`; `game.saves` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Action RPG / dungeon (Diablo, Landstalker) | `iso` | TileMap, FlowField, Body (jump onto blocks), GPU lighting | ADVENTURE |\n| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the screen; a second player drops in (`game.allowJoin`, `cam.frame` on both) | BRAWLER |\n| Fighting (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers) | `side` | two `E.Fighter`s in an `E.Match` (the fight module): moves with frame data, guards, throws, specials by motion (`'236'`) or charge, a meter, projectiles; `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`, training | FIGHTING |\n| Shoot-'em-up (1942, Gradius, R-Type) | `overhead` (vertical, and horizontal: world x scrolls) | sprites, Bullets, `E.pattern`, a timeline of waves; horizontal: rock edges as functions of x, a power bar, options on the ship's past path, `E.Path` loops; `E.Arcade` for the continue and the table | SHOOTER (both stages) |\n| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n| Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids) | `overhead` (one fixed screen, cabinet art on the sides) | `E.Arcade` (score, lives, extra lives, turns, initials, tables, attract mode); a maze of `E.GridMover`s; moths on `E.Path`s turned by `rot`; `E.wrap` and `wrap: [w, h]` | ARCADE |\n| Twin-stick / run-and-gun (Smash TV, Contra) | `topdown` / `side` | Body or Platformer, Bullets, `weapon: 'gun'`, `point: true` | SHOOTER + ADVENTURE |\n| JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, EarthBound) | `threequarter` town, `brawler` battles | TileMap towns and a big world map, the story and rpg modules, Dialog with markup, `game.saves` slots | RPG |\n| Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo, Columns) | `side` (a field in screen pixels) | a cell array, a bag from `E.rng`, `input.repeat` (auto-shift), `grid.groups` (chains), `input.drag()` and `clicked()` for touch; versus: two fields, rows sent across (`game.players`) | PUZZLE |\n| Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren) | `threequarter` / `iso` | `E.gen` floors, a TileMap of its rows, `E.Grid.from(map)` paths and `fov`, `E.Fog`, `E.Turns` by speed, `game.tween` steps | ROGUELIKE |\n| Tactics (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Fire Emblem) | `iso`, turned a quarter | TileMap of block heights, `map.pick` under the cursor, `E.Grid.from(map, { tops: true })` reach over heights, `grid.shape`, `grid.side`, `grid.threat`, `E.Turns` charge time, `E.Story` | TACTICS |\n# Objects and materials as data\n\nThe full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\nwith the house shading and outline, and gives every surface (floors, wall faces, wall tops, platform tiles, the objects'\nown faces) a material from one open registry. An object costs one to a few hundred tokens of data (the core's median is\n125); you check it headless with one command. Read this card whole before you write one. (The agent edition keeps the\nregistries and ignores the calls: `E.addAssets` returns empty lists, the others null.)\n\n## Use one\n\n```js\n// in draw(r): feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor; its front toward facing\nr.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n// once, before the updates: bodies stop at it, a body coming down lands on it, one wholly below passes under\nmap.solid('table', 120, 80, 0, { facing: 0 });\n// a sprite of it, for an inventory or a HUD (r.sprite, px.sprite)\nconst icon = E.shapeSprite('chest', { view: 'iso' });\n```\n\n- **r.shape options:** facing (radians, where the front points: 0 east, π/2 south, as written), scale, mats ({ slot:\n  material }), flip (mirrors it x to -x, collision too), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (default true),\n  light (adds its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true).\n- **map.solid** takes the same id and placement, so one object can feed both calls. Bodies span z to z + h (E.Body's h, 32).\n- **In 3D** the 3D engine draws the same entries, materials and boxes: `world.shape(id, x, y, z, o)` (its header).\n- **Steep views** (top-down) draw shapes from the characters' lower angle, as rigs are drawn. The light comes from the\n  viewer's upper left in every view.\n- **Glow and fire:** a material with glow: 1 ignores the light and stays bright in the dark; an entry's flames ([[x, y, z,\n  w, h]]) draw the engine's animated flame (r.shape only: a sprite has none). Anything else that moves stays a prop\n  (r.prop) or your own code.\n- **Dressing a generated level:** a scene is a few entries as [id, across, forward] from an anchor (a wall spot, forward\n  into the room); place it whole or not at all, each part on free floor, after the level's own random picks and from a\n  seeded stream of its own, so the level stays as its seed builds it (Emberdeep's `src/emberdeep/53-scenes.js`).\n\n## The core library\n\n**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\nbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\ntree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n\n**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\nbrick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\nplants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\nwalls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n\n## Materials on surfaces\n\n```js\nE.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\nconst types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\nconst map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\nconst level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n```\n\nfloorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n\nA material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\nevery surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\nOverlays, the last on top, each in its own color's tones: `over: [['moss', '#5f7a3a', { up: .6 }], ['cracks']]`; moss on\nwhat looks up, cracks (the material a step darker), dirt near the ground (h 6), rust; each takes amount and size.\n\n| Pattern | Numbers | What |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| none | | the light alone |\n| planks | bw 3, len 14, dir | boards with joints; staves on round parts; dir: 'v' turns them |\n| crate | frame 2, bw 3 | a framed, braced side; planks on its lid |\n| bricks | bw 6, bh 3, mortar | running bond |\n| stones | size 5 | irregular stones (Voronoi), dark joints, a lit rim |\n| tiles | size 4 | square tiles, grout |\n| speck, noise | amount .08; scale 4 | specks; soft patches |\n| foliage | size 3.5 | leaf clumps lit on top |\n| bark | | fissures; rings on a cut end |\n| metal | rivet | a shine where lit; rivets |\n| cloth | fold .9 | weave and folds |\n| glaze | | a glossy shine |\n| thatch, shingles | course; bw | straw courses; roof tiles |\n\nYour own pattern: `E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0` (s.u, s.v: world units\nacross and up the surface; s.lid, s.curved, s.lit, s.W, s.H; return a step, -1 to +2). A material may also paint one kind\nof surface its own way, per pixel: `face(wx, z, tones, type, cx, cy, fi, nh, h)` or `roof(wx, wy, tones, type)` returning\na color or null, `floor(x, y, tag, view)` returning [r, g, b].\n\n## Write one\n\nUnits: 16 = 1 m = one tile; x east, y south, z up. The origin is the middle of the footprint on the ground; write it\nfacing south (+y). Use whole or half units: a pixel at game size is about 0.7 units.\n\n```js\nE.SHAPES.stool = { about: 'round three-legged stool', tags: 'furniture tavern', mats: { w: 'oak', l: 'walnut' },\n  parts: [['cyl','w',[0,0,8],5,1.5], ['ring',3,3,['box','l',[0,0,0],[1.5,1.5,8],{rot:[0,-8,0]}]]] };\n```\n\nAn entry: `about`, `tags`, `mats` (slot to material; a slot name that is not in mats is a material itself), and `parts`, or\n`make(params)` returning parts with `params` its defaults. Optional: `scale` (times the placement's), `foot: [x0, y0,\nx1, y1]` (the footprint for collision, and for sorting when it stands raised; the bounds by default), `lights: [[x, y,\nz, color, radius]]`, `flames: [[x, y, z, w, h]]`.\n\n| Part | Form | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| box | `['box', m, at, [w, d, h], { rot }]` | at: the bottom middle |\n| cyl | `['cyl', m, at, r, h, { r2, seg, sq }]` | r2: top radius (0: a cone); sq squashes y; seg: 6 for a hexagon |\n| lathe | `['lathe', m, at, [[r, z], ...], { seg }]` | a profile turned about z, bottom to top; [0, z] closes an end |\n| ball | `['ball', m, at, r, { sz }]` | at: its centre; sz below 1 flattens it |\n| prism | `['prism', m, at, [[a, b], ...], h, { axis }]` | an outline pushed h: up z (outline x, y), or centred along y (outline x, z) or x (outline y, z) |\n| wedge | `['wedge', m, at, [w, d, h]]` | h tall at the back, down to the floor at the front |\n| rock | `['rock', m, at, r, { sz, seed, rough }]` | a lumpy, faceted ball; below the floor is not drawn |\n| use | `['use', id, at, { rot, scale, mats, ...params }]` | another shape inside this one |\n| mirror | `['mirror', 'x' \\| 'y' \\| 'xy', part]` | the part and its mirror copies |\n| ring, row | `['ring', n, radius, part]`, `['row', n, [dx, dy, dz], part]` | n copies round z (the part moved out to radius); n copies in a line, centred |\n| group | `['group', at, rot, [parts]]` | parts moved and turned together |\n\nEvery part takes `{ rot }`: a yaw in degrees, or [x, y, z] degrees. Write arrays densely (`[0,0,8]`, not `[0, 0, 8]`):\nspaces cost a third more tokens.\n\n### Worked entries\n\n```js\nbarrel: { about: 'oak barrel, two iron hoops', tags: 'container wood', mats: { w: 'oak', h: 'iron' },\n  parts: [['lathe','w',[0,0,0],[[0,0],[5,0],[6,3],[6.5,8],[6,13],[5,16],[0,16]]], ['row',2,[0,0,9],['cyl','h',[0,0,7.5],6.5,1.5]]] },\ncrate: { about: 'wooden crate, framed and braced', tags: 'container wood', mats: { c: 'crate' }, parts: [['box','c',[0,0,0],[15,15,14]]] },\ntable: { about: 'plank table, four legs', tags: 'furniture tavern', mats: { t: 'oak', l: 'walnut' },\n  parts: [['box','t',[0,0,10],[24,14,2]], ['mirror','xy',['box','l',[10,5,0],[2,2,10]]]] },\nchest: { about: 'oak chest, round lid, iron bands', tags: 'container treasure', mats: { w: 'oak', b: 'iron', l: 'gold' },\n  parts: [['box','w',[0,0,0],[16,10,8]], ['prism','w',[0,0,8],[[-5,0],[5,0],[4,3],[0,5],[-4,3]],16,{axis:'x'}],\n    ['mirror','x',['box','b',[5.5,0,0],[1.5,11,8.5]]], ['box','l',[0,5,5],[3,1,3]]] },\nlamppost: { about: 'iron street lamp, glowing head', tags: 'town light', mats: { m: 'iron', g: 'flame' }, lights: [[0,0,40,'#ffd070',70]],\n  parts: [['cyl','m',[0,0,0],2.5,3], ['cyl','m',[0,0,3],1,34], ['box','g',[0,0,37],[4,4,5]], ['cyl','m',[0,0,42],3.5,3,{r2:0,seg:4}]] },\nfence: { about: 'rail fence, len long (16)', tags: 'village farm', mats: { w: 'oak' }, params: { len: 16 },\n  make: p => [['mirror','x',['box','w',[p.len / 2 - 1,0,0],[2,2,12]]], ['row',2,[0,0,5],['box','w',[0,0,6],[p.len - 2,1,1.5]]]] },\n```\n\nA generator seeds its noise from its params (`E.rng(seed)`), never `Math.random`, so it draws the same pixels everywhere.\n\n## Make one: the recipe\n\n1. **Read this card whole.**\n2. **Find** the nearest entry: `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"tavern table\"` searches the core library and the store's sets\n   (`src/assets/sets/`, about a thousand objects, materials and sprites converted from CC0 libraries, each with where it\n   came from) and `--show set:id` prints one; the Asset Lab (`/asset-lab`) shows them all.\n3. **Copy** it and change its names, parts and materials, or write a new one from the parts above. Give the cue a player\n   knows it by parts of its own (a skep's coils as stacked rings, an anvil's horn, a barrow's open tub dark inside), and\n   keep small parts plain ('none', 'glaze'): a busy pattern on a part a few pixels wide reads as speckle.\n4. **Look:** `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` (a file that sets `E.SHAPES.stool`, or a store set; a core id\n   alone works too: `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs barrel`). It draws `check-output/asset-sheet/stool.png`: every view and\n   four facings, beside the hero, on a light and a dark floor. It lints what reads badly: too small from above, a part\n   under a pixel, too few tones, low contrast with the floor, its tokens. Read the picture, fix, repeat.\n5. **Use** it: `E.SHAPES.stool = {...}` and `r.shape('stool', ...)`; or a set file\n   (`(window.ASSETS = window.ASSETS || {}).MINE = { set: 'MINE', format: 1, materials, shapes }`) and\n   `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS.MINE)`, which names its entries 'MINE:stool' so they never collide, and returns the names.\n   A store set loads the same way (its script, then `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`);\n   `node tools/asset-set.mjs <sets> --ids a,b --name mine --out mine.js` cuts the few a game uses, with what they need\n   (Emberdeep's set dressing loads `src/assets/sets/emberdeep.js`, cut so).\n\n## Limits\n\n- Still objects. Lids that open, swinging signs and held weapons are code (or props) for now.\n- A shape sorts by one point, as props do; a long one (a bed, a cart) may cross a body walking right beside it.\n- Collision is the footprint's box, turned with the shape, and the bounds' height: a table is solid under its top too.\n- Bigger than about 240 pixels on screen, a shape skips the actors' effects (flash, x-ray).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat kits/adventure.js; cat game/game.js; cat game/test.mjs'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat kits/adventure.js; cat game/game.js; cat game/test.mjs'","aggregated_output":"// The ADVENTURE kit's game (a top-down action adventure: a village, ruins and a shrine, a sword, a key and a great door, talk with portraits; Zelda and Secret of Mana), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/10-adventure.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. adventure.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs adventure runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\nconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {};\nlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\nconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n];\n/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\nconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n});\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\nconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\nconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\nconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n];\nHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\nconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\nconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\nconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n  try {\n    if (fresh) fresh();\n    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n    return h >>> 0;\n  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n};\n// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\nconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\nconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n    const t = game.time;\n    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n    });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n    titleBg.draw(r);\n    stage.draw(r);\n    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n  }\n};\n\n/* ---- GAME OVER: shared by every slice ---- */\nconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\nconst overBg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#12040c', '#3a0c1c', '#6a1a28'], moon: { x: .5, y: .3, r: 16, color: '#e8a0a0' }, stars: 30,\n  layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#2a0c16', y: .72, height: .3, parallax: 0 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a2a3a', y: .9, height: .12, parallax: 0, drift: 4 }] });\nscenes.over = {\n  view: 'side', input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter(d) { overMenu.from = d.from; overMenu.i = 0; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); game.follow(null); game.focus(0, 0, 0); if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n  draw(r) {   // centred on any screen\n    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 60; overMenu.y = y + 58;\n    overBg.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: '#3a0810' })); overMenu.draw(r);\n  }\n};\n\n/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 1  ADVENTURE  (Secret of Mana, Zelda: ALttP). Three rooms: village, ruins, shrine. Talk, clear the ruins for\n * the key, open the great door, claim the crystal. THE LOOK: wall MATERIALS, ONE floorTex with PAINTED LIGHT, pitched\n * roofs, leaf-clump bushes, light shafts, dialog PORTRAITS.\n * KEYS: WASD or arrows move, J or X swings the sword, Enter or Space talks. TOUCH: the stick, ATTACK, CONFIRM.\n * ANY SCREEN: rooms are 4:3 in a world that goes on past them (forest above and below, the next rooms beside), so a\n * screen of any shape is filled. CAMERA (Settings, or C): ROOMS slides screen by screen as Zelda's does, the rooms beside\n * this one under a dim CURTAIN (they wait, as their monsters do); SCROLL follows the hero. The HUD sits in the corners.\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst ADV = (() => {\n  const T = 16, ROOM = [14 * T, 12 * T], AREAS = ['Mana Village', 'Mossy Ruins', 'Shrine of Mana'];\n  const ROWS = [\n    // village          ruins             shrine\n    ['^^^^^^^^^^^^^^', 'RRRRRRRRRRRRRR', 'XXXXXXXXXXXXXX'],\n    ['^^#^^^^^^^^#^^', 'RHhJKFYDYFKhHR', 'XwjiXnWXnXijwX'],\n    ['#UUUU.ZZZZ.~~#', 'R.u..qv.vq.S.R', 'X.S*.B..B.*S.X'],\n    ['#GQOQbzNzZu~~#', 'H.KK....x....H', 'X.....rA.....X'],\n    ['#ccccV~ccLe~~#', 'K..s.q::::.s.H', 'X..I..++..I..X'],\n    ['#cM@cPccac=~~#', 'H.....::::k..K', 'X....m++m....X'],\n    ['#,,,,,,,,,,__,', ',,....::C:...H', 'X4.I..++..I.4X'],\n    ['#.b...b.g,d__,', ',,..o.::::.s.H', 'X.....++.....X'],\n    ['#...%%%f..s~~#', 'Hb.K..::::q.KH', 'X..I..++..I..X'],\n    ['#T..%%%.u..~~#', 'H.u..s....y.RH', 'X.p...++...p.X'],\n    ['#.3........~~#', 'H...bK...b.xRH', 'X.....E+.....X'],\n    ['##############', 'RRRRRRRRRRRRRR', 'XXXXXX++XXXXXX']\n  ].map(r => r.join(''));\n  // the world AROUND the rooms: PAD rows of forest canopy above and below (a meadow's edge first, the shrine's stone under\n  // the shrine), so a screen of any shape is filled. The rooms' rows start at OY\n  const PAD = 12, OY = PAD * T, wood = (cx, cy) => cx >= 28 ? 'X' : E.hash2(cx * 7, cy * 5) < .18 ? '2' : '1';\n  const AROUND = (cy0, meadow) => Array.from({ length: PAD }, (_, i) => Array.from({ length: 42 }, (_, cx) => meadow && i < 2 && cx < 28 ? '.' : wood(cx, cy0 + i)).join(''));\n  ROWS.unshift(...AROUND(0)); ROWS.push(...AROUND(PAD + 12, true));\n  const LEGEND = {\n    // walls: a wall type (TYPES), or { tile, spawn } = a wall with a prop on its face (THINGS)\n    '#': 1, 'U': 5, 'Z': 8, 'R': 9, 'H': 3, 'K': 4, 'F': 6, 'X': 2, 'A': 7, '1': 10, '2': { tile: 10, spawn: 'tree' },\n    '^': { tile: 1, spawn: 'tree' }, 'G': { tile: 5, spawn: 'ivy' }, 'Q': { tile: 5, spawn: 'pane' }, 'O': { tile: 5, spawn: 'door' },\n    'z': { tile: 8, spawn: 'pane' }, 'N': { tile: 8, spawn: 'shop' }, 'h': { tile: 3, spawn: 'vines' }, 'J': { tile: 3, spawn: 'cobweb' }, 'Y': { tile: 6, spawn: 'moss' }, 'D': { tile: 6, spawn: 'gate' },\n    'w': { tile: 2, spawn: 'window' }, 'W': { tile: 2, spawn: 'rose' }, 'i': { tile: 2, spawn: 'torch' }, 'n': { tile: 2, spawn: 'banner' }, 'j': { tile: 2, spawn: 'cobweb' }, 'r': { tile: 7, spawn: 'relic' },\n    // floors: a tag for floorTex; block = not walkable\n    ',': { floor: 'path' }, 'c': { floor: 'plaza' }, '~': { floor: 'water', block: true }, '_': { floor: 'bridge' }, ':': { floor: 'pave' }, '+': { floor: 'carpet' }, '%': { floor: 'bed' },\n    '@': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'hero' }, 'M': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'elder' }, 'P': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'pot' }, 'L': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'lamp' },\n    'V': { floor: 'water', block: true, spawn: 'fountain' }, 'C': { floor: 'pave', spawn: 'chest' }, 'E': { floor: 'carpet', spawn: 'entry' }, 'd': { floor: 'path', spawn: 'villager' },\n    // people, creatures and props\n    'f': 'florist', 'a': { floor: 'plaza', spawn: 'cat' }, 's': 'rabite', 'v': 'bat', 'k': 'goblin', 'm': 'mage', 'b': 'bush', 'p': 'pot', 'T': 'oak', 'g': 'sign', 'u': 'mushroom',\n    'e': 'barrel', '=': 'crate', '3': 'stump', '4': 'obelisk', 'q': 'ruin', 'I': 'pillar', 'S': 'statue', 'o': 'rock', 'x': 'crystal', 'y': 'skull', 'B': 'brazier', '*': 'candelabra'\n  };\n  // wall MATERIALS: face = side, roof = top pattern (beam = timber); cut = lowered to cutH in front of the camera\n  const SLAB = { face: 'stone', roof: 'slab' }, TYPES = {\n    1: { h: 16, cut: true, cutH: 7, face: 'hedge', roof: 'leaves', top: '#3f8c3c', side: '#2e6a34' },   // hedge\n    2: { h: 34, cut: true, cutH: 8, ...SLAB, top: '#4e4670', side: '#6a6294', course: 9 },   // shrine stone\n    3: { h: 26, cut: true, cutH: 8, face: 'ruin', roof: 'slab', top: '#7a8a66', side: '#8e8a98' },   // ruin wall, mossy top: the 'ruin' MATERIAL (stones, cracks, moss, dirt; docs/ASSETS.md)\n    4: { h: 12, cut: true, ...SLAB, top: '#72845e', side: '#8e8a98', course: 6 },   // crumbled ruin\n    5: { h: 36, face: 'timber', roof: 'tiles', top: '#c4583a', side: '#f0e0c0', beam: '#6a4228' },   // cottage\n    6: { h: 36, ...SLAB, top: '#5a5480', side: '#7a7298', course: 9 },   // shrine facade\n    7: { h: 9, ...SLAB, top: '#8a84b4', side: '#5a5484', course: 4 },   // altar\n    8: { h: 36, face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', top: '#3a7ab4', side: '#f4e6c8' },   // shop\n    9: { h: 30, cut: true, cutH: 8, face: 'rock', roof: 'grass', top: '#5a9a44', side: '#8a7462' },   // cliff\n    10: { h: 22, face: 'hedge', roof: 'leaves', top: '#2c6a36', side: '#1f4a2a' }   // the forest round the rooms\n  };\n  // set dressing: tag -> prop(s). r = solid, cut = breakable (debris), drop = loot, face = on the wall at z (anchor\n  // 'top' hangs it), light = GPU light, dx = nudge, hidden = appears later; shape = a SHAPE (E.SHAPES, docs/ASSETS.md:\n  // right in every view and turn, no drawing code) in place of a prop, size its scale\n  const THINGS = {\n    // village\n    door: [{ face: true, size: 1.1, color: '#7a4222' }, { prop: 'lantern', face: true, z: 33, dx: 14, anchor: 'top', light: '#ffb060' }],\n    shop: [{ prop: 'door', face: true, size: 1.1, color: '#2a4a7a' }, { prop: 'awning', face: true, z: 23, size: .95, color: '#d8483a' }],\n    pane: { prop: 'window', face: true, z: 12, size: .65, color: '#6a4424', colors: ['#fff0b0', '#ffd070'] }, ivy: { prop: 'vines', face: true, z: 35, anchor: 'top', color: '#3a8a3a', blossom: '#f890b0' },\n    fountain: { prop: 'statue', size: .8, color: '#a8a6c0', dx: 8 }, lamp: { prop: 'streetlamp', r: 3, size: .8, halo: false }, oak: { prop: 'tree', size: 1.45, r: 8 },   // lamp: unlit by day\n    bush: { r: 6, cut: ['#2f7a34', '#5ab04a', '#9ad86a'] }, pot: { size: .95, r: 5, cut: ['#7a3a22', '#c07040', '#e8a878'], drop: 'gem' }, sign: { r: 4 },\n    mushroom: { size: .75, color: '#e0503a' }, barrel: { shape: 'barrel', r: 5, size: .75 }, crate: { shape: 'crate', r: 6, size: .65 },\n    // from the asset store, cut into the page's 'adventure' set (src/assets/sets/adventure.js); without it, props\n    ...(E.addAssets((window.ASSETS || {}).adventure || { set: 'adventure' }).shapes.length ? { stump: { shape: 'adventure:stump-round', r: 5, size: .7 },\n      obelisk: { shape: 'adventure:pillar-obelisk', r: 6, size: .8 } } : { stump: { prop: 'rock', r: 5, color: '#8a5a3a' }, obelisk: { prop: 'pillar', r: 6 } }),\n    // ruins\n    vines: { face: true, z: 25, anchor: 'top', color: '#4a8a3a', blossom: '#f890b0' }, moss: { prop: 'vines', face: true, z: 35, anchor: 'top', size: .8, color: '#5a8a3a', blossom: '#f890b0' },\n    gate: { prop: 'door', face: true, size: 1.1, color: '#5a3a6a' }, ruin: { prop: 'pillar', broken: true, r: 7 }, rock: { r: 5, color: '#8a8698' }, skull: { prop: 'bones' },\n    crystal: { r: 4, light: '#5ad8f0' }, chest: { r: 6, hidden: true },\n    // shrine\n    window: { face: true, z: 7, size: .8, colors: ['#e05a6a', '#5a8ae8', '#f0c85a', '#6ad08a'], light: '#8ab0ff' }, torch: { face: true, z: 14, light: '#ff9a4a' },\n    rose: { prop: 'window', face: true, z: 2, size: 1, dx: 8, colors: ['#e8c85a', '#c04aa0', '#5a8ae8'], light: '#c8a0ff' }, banner: { face: true, z: 8, size: .8, color: '#8a1a3a', emblem: '#e8c04a' },\n    cobweb: { face: true, z: 34, anchor: 'top', size: .9 }, pillar: { r: 7 }, statue: { r: 6, color: '#9a98b0' }, brazier: { r: 5, size: .9, light: '#ff9a4a' }, candelabra: { r: 3, size: .8, light: '#ffc060' }\n  };\n  // palettes: E.ramp(hex, n, strength) = n hue-shifted shades, dark to light\n  const rgb = hexes => hexes.map(E.hex), R5 = (c, s = .6) => rgb(E.ramp(c, 5, s)), FLAG = (s, mortar) => ({ stones: s.slice(1, 4), mortar, hi: s[4], lo: s[0], speck: s[1] });\n  const GRASS = [['#4c9a3e', '#5aa640', '#6cb44c'], ['#42804a', '#4a8a48', '#5a9a4e']].map(room => room.map(c => R5(c))), DIRT = R5('#b08652', .7), WATER = R5('#2a7ac4', .9), STONE = R5('#a49a8a', .7), SOIL = R5('#6e4a34');\n  const PLAZA = FLAG(R5('#b4a894'), E.hex('#6a5e52')), PAVE = FLAG(R5('#8a8a96'), E.hex('#3a3a3e')), TILE = [R5('#5a5688'), R5('#403c68')], PETAL = rgb(['#ffffff', '#ffe070', '#f890b0']);\n  const CARPET = rgb(E.ramp('#9a2438', 4)), GOLD = rgb(E.ramp('#d8a840', 3)), RUNE = [...E.hex('#6ae8e0'), .35], LILY = R5('#4aa050');   // 4th value = GPU glow\n  const SKY = rgb(['#a8dcf4', '#e8f8ff']), REFLECT = E.hex('#1e5a5a');   // sky glints, the hedge's reflection\n  const TUFT = ['.l.l.', '.dld.', '..d..'], BLOOM = ['.w.', 'wyw', '.w.'];   // grass stamps\n  const MOOD = [[.92, .9, .84], [.8, .88, .8], [.34, .3, .46]];   // GPU ambient light per room\n  const mood = m => { if (gpu) gpu.ambient = m; L.ambient = (m[0] + m[1] + m[2]) / 3; };   // (and the canvas lighting's, where WebGPU is missing and it stands in)\n  // light shafts per room: beam x, tint (a dark tint = a faint beam), lean\n  const BEAMS = [[[34, 128, 196], '#7a5a26', 60], [[50, 150], '#566a22', 60], [[24, 120, 200], '#4a3a8a', 12]];\n  const WIN = { bg: ['#3a4a9e', '#12163e'], border: '#f0e0a8' }, FACE_BG = ['#7aa4e8', '#1e2a66'];\n  // pixel sprites ('.' = transparent)\n  const GEM = E.sprite(['..g..', '.gGg.', 'gGWGg', 'gGGGg', 'dgGgd', '.dgd.', '..d..'], { g: '#1e9a3a', G: '#56e070', W: '#e8fff0', d: '#0e5a24' });\n  const HEART = E.sprite(['.R.R.', 'RWRRR', 'RRRRR', '.RRR.', '..R..'], { R: '#e8384a', W: '#ffd0d6' });\n  const KEYS = [1, 2].map(s => E.sprite(['.yy....', 'y..y...', 'Y..Yyyy', '.YY..y.', '.....yY'], { y: '#f8d048', Y: '#b07818' }, s));   // scale 2: held up high\n  const CRYSTALS = [1, 2].map(s => E.sprite(['....w....', '...wWc...', '..wWWcc..', '.wWWWccC.', 'wWWWccccC', '.wWWcccC.', '.cWWccCC.', '..cWcCC..', '..ccCC...', '...cC....'], { w: '#f0ffff', W: '#a8f0ff', c: '#4ac8e8', C: '#2a5ab0' }, s));\n\n  // THE CAST: chibi rigs, anime eyes, own outfits and palettes; the hero's cape is SECONDARY MOTION\n  const RIGS = {\n    hero: () => new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', face: { eyes: 'big', bangs: .8 }, cape: { len: 4, width: 3.2, seg: 2.2 },\n      colors: { skin: '#f8cca4', hair: '#e8902c', cloth: '#3a8a4a', trim: '#f0d070', pants: '#4a3a5a', boot: '#8a4a26', belt: '#6a3a1a', glove: '#7a5238', eye: '#3a2a6a', cape: '#d0483a', capeIn: '#7a1e2e' } }),\n    elder: () => new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'short', sleeves: 'long', hunch: .45, hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3e3278' }, face: { eyes: 'big', bangs: .35 },\n      colors: { skin: '#f0c4a8', hair: '#b8b2c4', cloth: '#5a4a9a', trim: '#f0cc60', belt: '#f0cc60', boot: '#4a3a2a', eye: '#2a2a4a' } }),\n    florist: () => new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.15, weapon: null, outfit: 'robe', sleeves: 'long', hair: 'ponytail', face: { eyes: 'big', bangs: 1 },\n      colors: { skin: '#f8cca4', hair: '#b0482a', cloth: '#d86a8a', trim: '#f4a8c0', belt: '#fff0d0', pants: '#d86a8a', boot: '#6a3a2a', eye: '#2a5a3a' } }),\n    villager: () => new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.1, weapon: null, hair: 'short', hat: { style: 'band', color: '#d8483a' }, face: { eyes: 'big', bangs: .7 }, shoulderHalf: 4.6, armUpper: 5.2, armLower: 5,   // the wave clears his face\n      colors: { skin: '#f0c090', hair: '#6a3a1e', cloth: '#e8a83a', trim: '#fff0d0', pants: '#4a5a8a', boot: '#6a4a2a', belt: '#6a4a2a', eye: '#2a3a5a' } }),\n    goblin: () => new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.1, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'bald', eyeGlow: '#ffd84a',\n      colors: { skin: '#8ab84a', cloth: '#8a5a32', trim: '#c8a040', pants: '#4a3a2a', boot: '#3a2a1a', belt: '#3a2a1a' } }),\n    mage: () => new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hood: true, sleeves: 'long', eyeGlow: '#ff6ab0',\n      colors: { skin: '#c8b8e0', hair: '#2e2450', cloth: '#4a3a86', trim: '#d070f0', belt: '#d070f0', boot: '#1a1628', orb: '#ff80e0' } })\n  };\n  // BLOB CREATURES: a round body plus parts\n  const RABITE = { dk: '#b0703a', base: '#f4d49a', lt: '#fff4dc', pupil: '#5a1a2a', inner: '#f09aa8', ext: '#d8a060' };\n  const BAT = { dk: '#2e1a44', base: '#6a4a9a', lt: '#a890d0', eye: '#fff0a0', pupil: '#c02020', wing: '#4a2a6a', inner: '#e08aa0' };\n  const CAT = { dk: '#9a5028', base: '#f0a050', lt: '#ffd8a0', pupil: '#2a4a1a', inner: '#f8b0b0', ext: '#fff0e0' };\n  const FOES = {   // hp (a hit does 8-12), look, moves (E.MOVES with a long, deep wind-up: the TELL)\n    rabite: { hp: 18, look: () => new E.Blob({ R: 5.5, colors: RABITE, ears: 'rabbit', feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true, face: 'front' }) },\n    bat: { hp: 12, fly: 17, look: () => new E.Blob({ R: 4.5, colors: BAT, wings: true, ears: 'cat', mouth: 'fangs', face: 'front' }) },\n    goblin: { hp: 40, look: RIGS.goblin, moves: ['claw', 'twohand'], tune: { wind: .34, crouch: 1, lean: .9 } },   // a raking claw, a two-fist SLAM\n    mage: { hp: 30, look: RIGS.mage, moves: ['cast'], tune: { wind: .6, lean: .6 } }   // leans back to raise, recoils forward to release\n  };\n  // spins at the waist; CHARGE: the spin's wind-up, deeper\n  const WAIST = { z0: -10, z1: -10 }, CHARGE = { ...E.MOVES.spin, ...WAIST, a0: 2.4, crouch: .6, lean: .6 };\n  // idle: poses in turn; near: turn to the hero (wave: say hello); talk: gestures; chore: a move while kneeling\n  const NPCS = {\n    elder: { name: 'ELDER', idle: [null, null, 'hips'], near: 56, talk: ['block', null, 'hips', null], lines: [() => 'Rabites overran the Mossy Ruins across the river. Press ' + game.input.label('attack') + ' to swing your sword and clear them out!',\n      'Clear the ruins and the old chest opens. The Mana crystal sleeps in the shrine behind the great door.'] },\n    florist: { name: 'LISE', face: Math.PI, idle: ['kneel', 'kneel', null], near: 36, talk: ['hips', 'cast'],   // tends the flower bed\n      chore: () => new E.Attack('plunge', { hand: 'both', a0: -.5, a1: -.9, r0: 4, r1: 9, wind: .3, active: .16, recover: .45 }),\n      lines: ['A rabite got into my garden again! Could you shoo it away?', 'Mind the bats in the ruins. They swoop when you get close!'] },\n    villager: { name: 'PIP', idle: [null, 'hips'], near: 50, wave: true, talk: ['hips', null], lines: ['Hi! The bridge leads to the Mossy Ruins.', () => 'Keep ' + game.input.label('attack') + ' held after a swing, then let go: a SPIN ATTACK!'] }   // a function: the player's own key\n  };\n  // BACKDROP (iso view): a sea of clouds\n  const bg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#3a74c8', '#8ac2ea', '#e4f2f4', '#9ccae6', '#5a90c8'], layers: [{ kind: 'clouds', color: '#ffffff', y: .3, height: .16, parallax: .04, drift: 3 },\n    { kind: 'clouds', color: '#ffffff', y: .98, height: .4, parallax: .1, drift: 3, seed: 9 }] });\n  let map, relic, entry, hero, npcs, foes, pets, items, things, roofs, shots, talk, speaker, won, keys, gems, area, held, fx;\n  // CAMERA, the player's choice: 'rooms' slides screen by screen (Zelda), 'scroll' follows the hero (Settings, or C)\n  game.settings.define({ key: 'advCamera', group: 'Adventure', label: 'Camera', options: [['rooms', 'Rooms'], ['scroll', 'Scroll']], value: 'rooms', help: 'Rooms: screen by screen, as Zelda. Scroll: it follows the hero' });\n  // LIGHTING: GPU lights (pools of light and shadows, WebGPU) draw every frame twice and light each pixel: a phone's frame\n  // rate pays for them, so Auto keeps them for a computer (its main pointer a mouse or touchpad) and a phone gets Fast (the\n  // floor is lit already): the main pointer, as a phone with a stylus has a fine one too\n  const gpuWanted = () => game.settings.advLight === 'gpu' || (game.settings.advLight === 'auto' && !!(window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(pointer: fine)').matches));\n  const lighting = () => { if (!map) return; if (gpuWanted() && !gpu) gpu = game.enableGPU({ map }); if (gpu) Object.assign(gpu, { map, enabled: gpuWanted(), bands: 24, wrap: .5 }); };\n  game.settings.define({ key: 'advLight', group: 'Adventure', label: 'Lighting', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['gpu', 'GPU'], ['fast', 'Fast']], value: 'auto', help: 'GPU: pools of light and shadows (slow on a phone). Fast: smooth on a phone. Auto: GPU on a computer, Fast on a phone', apply: () => { if (game.sceneName === 'adventure') lighting(); } });\n  addEventListener('keydown', e => { if (e.code !== 'KeyC' || e.repeat || game.sceneName !== 'adventure' || game.paused) return; const v = game.settings.advCamera === 'rooms' ? 'scroll' : 'rooms'; game.settings.set('advCamera', v); game.note('CAMERA: ' + v.toUpperCase()); });\n  const sliding = () => !!game.cam.room && game.cam.moving;   // a room slide holds the world still\n  const roomOf = x => Math.floor(x / ROOM[0]), mod = (a, n) => ((a % n) + n) % n, near = (cx, cy, tag) => map.floorAt((cx + .5) * T, (cy + .5) * T) === tag;\n  const txt = (g, s, x, y, c, o) => E.font.text(g, s, x, y, c, { shadow: '#07040c', outline: false, ...o });\n  const talkable = () => npcs.find(n => E.dist(hero, n) < 34);\n  // CONTACT SHADOWS: a darker core in a soft ellipse, cool purple\n  const shadow = (r, x, y, rad) => { r.shadow(x, y, rad, .28, '#2a2048'); r.shadow(x, y, rad * .6, .22, '#2a2048'); };\n\n  /* ---- FLOORS: floorTex(x, y, tag) = [r, g, b(, glow)], baked once per view ---- */\n  // AUTOTILING: distance to the nearest side bordering another floor, corners rounded by K\n  function edge(cx, cy, lx, ly, tag, K) {\n    const o = (dx, dy) => { const t = map.floorAt((cx + dx + .5) * T, (cy + dy + .5) * T), c = map.cell(cx + dx, cy + dy); return tag === 'water' ? t !== tag && t !== 'bridge' && !c : t !== tag || c !== 0; };\n    const a = Math.min(o(-1, 0) ? lx : 99, o(1, 0) ? T - lx : 99), b = Math.min(o(0, -1) ? ly : 99, o(0, 1) ? T - ly : 99);\n    return a < K && b < K ? K - Math.hypot(K - a, K - b) : Math.min(a, b);\n  }\n  // GRASS: TUFT and BLOOM stamps on a staggered lattice in SCREEN pixels\n  function grass(sx, sy, G) {\n    const row = Math.floor(sy / 7), X = sx + (row & 1) * 6, k = E.hash2(Math.floor(X / 12), row), pat = k < .07 ? BLOOM : k < .62 ? TUFT : null;\n    const ch = pat && (pat[mod(Math.floor(sy), 7) - 2] || '')[mod(Math.floor(X), 12) - (pat === BLOOM ? 5 : 4)];\n    return ch === 'l' ? G[3] : ch === 'd' ? G[1] : ch === 'y' ? PETAL[1] : ch === 'w' ? PETAL[k < .035 ? 0 : 2] : G[2];\n  }\n  function ground(x, y, tag) {\n    const cx = Math.floor(x / T), cy = Math.floor(y / T), lx = x - cx * T, ly = y - cy * T, room = roomOf(x), [sx, sy] = game.view.p(x, y), h = E.hash2(cx, cy);\n    const e = tag && tag !== 'carpet' ? edge(cx, cy, lx, ly, tag, tag === 'water' ? 7 : tag === 'pave' ? 1 : 4) : 99;\n    if (e < 0) tag = null;   // outside a rounded corner\n    // WATER: bank, lip, shadow, reflection, foam, then depth BANDS bent by value noise\n    if (tag === 'water') {\n      if (e < 2.6) return e < 1 ? STONE[0] : E.hash2(Math.floor(y / 3), cx) < .2 ? STONE[1] : STONE[e < 1.8 ? 4 : 3];\n      const w = (E.noise2(x / 6, y / 9) - .5) * 5, foam = near(cx, cy - 1, 'bridge') ? ly : near(cx, cy + 1, 'bridge') ? T - ly : 99;\n      if (e < 3.3 || foam < 3 + w + E.hash2(Math.floor(sx / 2), 1) * 2) return foam < 1.5 + w ? SKY[1] : WATER[4];\n      if (!near(cx - 1, cy, 'water') && lx < 6 + w) return WATER[0];\n      if (map.cell(cx + 1, cy) > 0 && lx > 11 + w) return REFLECT;\n      const px_ = lx - 4 - h * 8, py_ = ly - 4 - h * 7, pad = Math.hypot(px_, py_);\n      if (h < .3 && pad < 3) return LILY[pad < 1 ? 4 : px_ > .5 && Math.abs(py_) < .5 ? 1 : 2];\n      const k = mod(Math.floor(sx) + Math.floor(sy / 6) * 7, 23);   // sky glints on every 6th row\n      return mod(Math.floor(sy), 6) === 0 && k < 4 ? SKY[k ? 0 : 1] : WATER[e + w < 8 ? 3 : e + w < 12 ? 2 : 1];\n    }\n    if (tag === 'bridge') return (ly < 2 && !near(cx, cy - 1, tag)) || (ly > T - 2 && !near(cx, cy + 1, tag)) ? DIRT[0] : E.tex.planks(y, x, { base: '#b07c44', dark: '#8a5c32', line: '#4a2e1a' });\n    // path and paving: grass erodes the edge by a hash; dirt, pebbles\n    const q = E.hash2(Math.floor(sx / 6), Math.floor(sy / 5)), b = E.hash2(Math.floor(x / 4), Math.floor(y / 4)) * 3;\n    if (tag === 'path') return e < b ? grass(sx, sy, GRASS[room][1]) : e < b + .9 ? DIRT[0] : q < .16 && mod(Math.floor(sx), 6) < 2 && mod(Math.floor(sy), 5) === 0 ? DIRT[q < .07 ? 4 : 1] : DIRT[e < b + 1.8 ? 1 : 2];\n    if (tag === 'plaza') return e < .9 ? PLAZA.mortar : E.tex.flagstone(x, y, PLAZA, 8);\n    if (tag === 'bed') return e < 1 ? STONE[0] : e < 2.4 ? STONE[3] : SOIL[mod(ly, 4) < 1 ? 0 : 2];\n    const c = Math.min(near(cx - 1, cy, tag) ? 99 : lx, near(cx + 1, cy, tag) ? 99 : T - lx), m = Math.abs(mod(x, 32) - 16) + Math.abs(ly - 8);   // carpet\n    if (tag === 'carpet') return c < 1 ? CARPET[0] : c >= 2 && c < 3 ? GOLD[1] : m > 5 && m < 6.5 ? GOLD[0] : m < 2.5 ? GOLD[2] : CARPET[1];\n    const f = E.tex.flagstone(x, y, PAVE);   // paving: moss in the seams\n    if (tag === 'pave') return e < b ? grass(sx, sy, GRASS[1][1]) : e < b + .9 ? PAVE.mortar : f === PAVE.mortar && E.hash2(Math.floor(x / 6), Math.floor(y / 6)) < .45 ? GRASS[1][1][1] : f;\n    const n = E.noise2(x / 40 + room * 9, y / 40);   // lawn: three shades in slow patches\n    if (room < 2) return grass(sx, sy, GRASS[room][n < .36 ? 0 : n > .64 ? 2 : 1]);\n    const dr = Math.hypot(x - relic.x, y - relic.y), a = Math.atan2(y - relic.y, x - relic.x), P = TILE[(cx + cy) & 1];\n    if (Math.abs(dr - 15) < .7 || Math.abs(dr - 10.5) < .6 || (dr > 11 && dr < 14.5 && Math.abs(mod(a / Math.PI * 4, 1) - .5) < .06)) return RUNE;   // shrine: a rune circle...\n    if (dr < 26) return dr > 24.8 ? TILE[1][0] : dr > 23.2 ? TILE[0][4] : TILE[dr < 20 ? 1 : 0][2];   // ...on a round dais with a lit rim...\n    if (Math.min(lx, ly) < 1.2) return P[lx < .8 || ly < .8 ? 0 : 4];   // ...on marble tiles\n    return lx > T - 1.2 || ly > T - 1.2 ? P[1] : mod(lx + ly, 13) < 1 ? P[3] : P[2];\n  }\n  // PAINTED LIGHT (Legend of Mana): a wall taller than its distance toward the low sun shades a point cool purple\n  const SHADE = [.64, .68, .86];\n  function floorTex(x, y, tag) {\n    const c = ground(x, y, tag);\n    for (let d = 2; d < 18; d += 2) if (map.heightAt(x - d, y - d * .3) > d * 1.8) return c.map((v, i) => i < 3 ? v * SHADE[i] : v);\n    return c;\n  }\n\n  // trees and pines varied by hashes\n  const tree = (cx, cy, pine) => { const v = E.hash2(cx * 5, cy * 3); return { prop: pine || v > .72 ? 'pine' : 'tree', size: 1 + v * .45, color: ['#2f7a3c', '#3f8a45', '#2a6a44', '#4a8a3a'][Math.floor(v * 4)], x: (cx + .3 + E.hash2(cy, cx) * .4) * T }; };\n  function start() {\n    map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ROWS, legend: LEGEND, types: TYPES, floorTex, ao: 8 });\n    relic = map.find('relic'); entry = map.find('entry'); relic.x += T / 2; entry.x += T / 2;   // on the room's center line\n    // the camera stays inside the map (the forest round the rooms fills a tall screen); update() sets rooms or scroll\n    game.cam.bounds = v => { const b = map.bounds(v); return { x0: b.x0 + 9, y0: b.y0 + 9, x1: b.x1 - 9, y1: b.y1 - 9 }; }; game.cam.room = game.settings.advCamera === 'scroll' ? null : ROOM;\n    const at = map.find('hero');\n    // SWORD (Secret of Mana): J chains slash, backslash, spin, kept low (a raised blade crosses his face); short holds (hold)\n    // let the follow-through settle instead of freezing; hold J to CHARGE\n    hero = Object.assign(new E.Body({ ...at, r: 4.5 }), { hp: 3, max: 3, facing: Math.PI / 2, inv: 0, hurt: 0, charge: 0, rig: RIGS.hero(),\n      combo: new E.Combo([new E.Attack('slash', { z0: -8, z1: -11, a1: -1.2, wind: .12, hold: .1 }), new E.Attack('backslash', { z0: -11, z1: -9, a1: 1.2, hold: .1 }), new E.Attack('spin', { ...WAIST, hold: .15 })], { window: .3 }),\n      spin: new E.Attack('spin', { ...WAIST, active: .36, reach: 10, lean: .3, hold: .12 }) });\n    hero.sw = hero.combo;   // the attack running now\n    npcs = Object.keys(NPCS).map(k => { const n = Object.assign({ said: 0, t: 0, k: 0, hi: 0, nod: 0, face: Math.PI / 2, rig: RIGS[k]() }, map.find(k), NPCS[k]); n.dir = n.look = n.face; n.job = n.chore && n.chore(); return n; });\n    things = [];\n    for (const s of map.spawns) for (const d of [].concat(s.tag === 'tree' ? tree(s.cx, s.cy) : THINGS[s.tag] || []))\n      things.push(Object.assign({ tag: s.tag, prop: s.tag, x: s.x + (d.dx || 0), y: s.y, room: roomOf(s.x) }, d));\n    // one pass over the cells: roofs, pines, weeds, flower beds, bridge rails, tufts\n    const box = {};\n    for (let cy = 0; cy < map.h - 1; cy++) for (let cx = 0; cx < map.w; cx++) {\n      const c = map.cell(cx, cy), v = E.hash2(cx * 3, cy * 7 + 1), X = (cx + .5) * T, Y = (cy + .5) * T, tag = map.floorAt(X, Y), add = o => things.push(Object.assign({ x: X, y: Y }, o));\n      if (c === 5 || c === 8) { const b = box[c] || (box[c] = [cx, cy, cx, cy]); b[2] = cx; b[3] = cy; }\n      if (map.spawns.some(s => s.cx === cx && s.cy === cy)) continue;\n      if (c === 9 && cy === PAD && v < .5) add(tree(cx, cy, true));\n      else if ((c === 3 || c === 4) && v < .45) add({ prop: 'bush', size: .7 + v * .6, color: '#5a8a44' });\n      else if (tag === 'bed') {\n        for (const k of [-3, 3]) add({ prop: 'flowers', size: 1.1, x: X + k, y: Y + k, color: k < 0 ? ['#f06a9a', '#f0a040', '#ffffff'][cx % 3] : '#8ab0ff', color2: '#fff4a0' });\n        if (!near(cx, cy + 1, 'bed')) add({ prop: 'fence', size: 1.2, y: Y + 8, color: '#b08050' });\n      }\n      else if (tag === 'bridge') for (const s of [-1, 1]) { if (!near(cx, cy + s, 'bridge')) add({ prop: 'fence', size: 1.2, y: Y + s * 7, color: '#8a5a32' }); }\n      else if (!c && !tag && X < 2 * ROOM[0] && v < .16) add({ prop: v < .06 ? 'flowers' : 'grass', x: X + (E.hash2(cx, cy) - .5) * 10, y: Y + (E.hash2(cy, cx) - .5) * 8,\n        color: v < .06 ? '#f06a9a' : X > ROOM[0] ? '#5a9a4a' : '#6ab850', color2: '#fff4a0' });\n    }\n    roofs = Object.keys(box).map(id => { const [a, b, c, d] = box[id]; return { x0: a * T, y0: b * T, x1: (c + 1) * T, y1: (d + 1) * T, h: TYPES[id].h, C: E.ramp(TYPES[id].top, 5) }; });\n    items = [{ kind: 'relic', x: relic.x, y: relic.y }];\n    // bats roost (hang; wake = time since); stun = flinch; dying = death; streak = claw marks; hold = an impact frame\n    foes = Object.keys(FOES).flatMap(k => map.findAll(k)).map(s => { const F = FOES[s.tag], moves = (F.moves || []).map(m => new E.Attack(m, { recover: .45, hold: .5, ...F.tune }));\n      return Object.assign(new E.Body({ ...s, r: 5.5, friction: 6, ...(F.fly && { z: F.fly + 8, gravity: 0, onGround: false }) }), { kind: s.tag, hp: F.hp, fly: F.fly, hang: !!F.fly, home: { ...s },\n        t: 1 + Math.random(), flash: 0, stun: 0, swoop: 0, wake: 9, streak: [], face: Math.PI / 2, room: roomOf(s.x), look: F.look(), moves, atk: moves[0] }); });\n    pets = map.findAll('cat').map(s => Object.assign(new E.Body({ ...s, r: 4 }), { t: 1, home: { ...s }, look: new E.Blob({ R: 4, colors: CAT, ears: 'cat', tail: true, feet: true, mouth: true, face: 'front' }) }));\n    shots = new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' }); talk = new E.Dialog(game, WIN);\n    fx = []; won = false; keys = 0; gems = 0; area = { room: 0, t: 2.6 }; held = null;\n    // the floor is lit already; GPU lighting (if any) adds light pools and shadows\n    L.enabled = false; lighting(); mood(MOOD[0]); A.music('adventure');\n    game.input.touchSet('attack', 'SWORD');\n  }\n  // DIALOG: E.Dialog types and pages; portrait: a live close-up of the speaker\n  const say = (who, name, text) => { speaker = who; talk.say(typeof text === 'function' ? text() : text, { name, portrait: who.rig, portraitSize: 50, portraitOpts: { zoom: 2.6, turn: -.25, cape: false, bg: FACE_BG } }); };   // (at the bottom, clear of the touch buttons)\n  function hurtHero(ang) {   // flinch, knockback, blink; true if it hurt\n    if (hero.inv > 0 || won || hero.hp <= 0) return false; hero.hp -= .5; hero.inv = 1; hero.hurt = .25; hero.charge = 0; hero.combo.cancel(); hero.spin.cancel(); hero.push(Math.cos(ang) * 160, Math.sin(ang) * 160);\n    game.hitFx(hero.x + Math.cos(ang) * 3, hero.y + Math.sin(ang) * 3, 12, { power: .9, angle: ang + Math.PI, color: '#ff8a6a', sound: 'hurt' }); game.flash('#ff4a3a', .06, .4);\n    if (hero.hp <= 0) { poof(hero.x, hero.y, 0, 1.2); game.after(.8, () => game.go('over', { from: 'adventure' })); }\n    return true;\n  }\n  const shiver = k => Math.sin(game.time * 90) * k;   // a tremble (tells, charging)\n  // a sword hit (k = power): game.hitFx, a FLINCH (stun, squash, hurt pose), knockback; the last starts the death\n  function strike(f, k = 1) {\n    const h = hero, an = E.angleTo(h, f), dmg = Math.round(E.randInt(8, 12) * k);\n    f.hp -= dmg; f.dmg = dmg; f.hitT = game.time; f.flash = .06; f.stun = .3; f.swoop = 0; f.aim = null; if (f.atk) f.atk.cancel(); f.look.kick(-6);\n    E.knockback(h, f, (f.hp > 0 ? 220 : 100) * k, f.fly ? 0 : f.hp > 0 || f.moves.length ? 60 : 140);   // a dead rabite pops up\n    game.hitFx(lerp(h.x, f.x, .6), lerp(h.y, f.y, .6), 10 + f.z * .5, { angle: an, power: k });\n    if (f.hp <= 0) { f.dying = f.fly ? .6 : f.moves.length ? 1.2 : .7; f.gravity = 700; f.hang = false; game.freeze(.1); A.sfx('stomp'); }\n  }\n  function vanish(f) {   // after the death animation: a poof, bits and a drop\n    f.dead = true; poof(f.x, f.y, f.z, f.kind === 'mage' ? 1.4 : 1);\n    if (f.kind === 'mage') { P.glints(f.x, f.y, 14, 8, '#f0b0ff', 18); game.flash('#f0d0ff', .08, .5); A.sfx('explode', { pitch: 1.3 }); }\n    else P.bits(f.x, f.y, 6 + f.z, 14, f.look instanceof E.Blob ? [f.look.C.dk, f.look.C.base, f.look.C.lt] : ['#8ab84a', '#8a5a32', '#c8d0d8']);\n    items.push({ kind: hero.hp < hero.max && E.chance(.5) ? 'heart' : 'gem', x: f.x, y: f.y });\n  }\n  // push bodies out of solid props\n  const settle = b => { for (const t of things) if (t.r && !t.dead && !t.hidden) { const dx = b.x - t.x, dy = b.y - t.y, dd = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1, m = b.r + t.r; if (dd < m) { b.x = t.x + dx / dd * m; b.y = t.y + dy / dd * m; } } };\n  // prize: face the camera and CHEER. Charging holds CHARGE's wind-up, deeper as it builds\n  function poseHero(dt) {\n    const h = hero, cheer = held && held.t > 0, still = talk.open || sliding() || cheer, v = game.view;\n    h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: h.y, z: h.z, vx: still ? 0 : h.vx, vy: still ? 0 : h.vy, facing: cheer ? Math.atan2(v.fy, v.fx) : h.facing, hurt: h.hurt > 0, pose: cheer ? 'cheer' : null,\n      attack: cheer ? null : h.charge > .15 ? { spec: CHARGE, phase: 'wind', u: Math.min(1, (h.charge - .15) / .45) } : h.sw.state });\n  }\n  // NPCS LIVE: idle poses, glances, chores; turn to the hero when near (a hello per visit); gesture and nod when speaking\n  function npcLife(n, dt) {\n    const d = E.dist(hero, n), near = d < n.near, says = talk.open && speaker === n, g = says && n.talk[Math.floor(game.real / .9) % n.talk.length];\n    if ((n.t -= dt) <= 0) { n.t = E.rand(2, 4.5); n.pose = n.idle[n.k++ % n.idle.length]; n.look = n.face + E.rand(-.7, .7) * (n.job && n.pose ? .3 : 1); }   // at work: eyes on the work\n    if (n.wave && near && !n.met) n.hi = 2;\n    n.met = near || n.met && d < n.near + 24; n.hi -= dt;   // waves again after he left\n    if ((n.hi > 0 || says && talk.typing) && (n.nod -= dt) <= 0) { n.nod = n.hi > 0 ? .57 : E.rand(.25, .45); n.rig.kick(-2.5); }   // a nod every few words, a bob per wave\n    const job = n.job && n.pose && !near && n.job;   // pats the soil, pauses, pats\n    if (job) { if (!job.busy && Math.random() < dt * 1.5) job.start(); job.update(dt); }\n    // a hello faces the camera, a speaker mostly (a stage actor): gestures clear the face\n    const cam = Math.atan2(game.view.fy, game.view.fx), to = E.angleTo(n, hero);\n    n.dir = E.approachAng(n.dir, n.hi > 0 ? cam : says ? to + E.angDiff(to, cam) * .6 : near ? to : n.look, dt * 6);\n    n.rig.update(dt, { x: n.x, y: n.y, facing: n.dir, pose: g || (n.hi > 0 ? 'wave' : near ? null : n.pose), expr: (n.hi > 0 || says) && 'smile', attack: job ? job.state : null });\n  }\n  function update(dt) {\n    const h = hero, room = roomOf(h.x), inp = game.input, npc = talkable();\n    inp.touchSet('confirm', talk.open ? 'NEXT' : 'TALK', talk.open || !!npc);   // a CONTEXT button: there only when there is someone to talk to\n    if (held) held.t -= dt;\n    for (const n of npcs) npcLife(n, dt);\n    if (talk.update(dt)) { poseHero(dt); return; }   // dialog pauses the world\n    mood(MOOD[room]);\n    if (room !== area.room) area = { room, t: 2.6 }; else area.t -= dt;\n    if (sliding() || won || held && held.t > 0) { poseHero(dt); return; }   // the room slides or the hero cheers\n    h.inv -= dt; h.hurt -= dt; if (h.hp <= 0) return;\n    if (npc && inp.pressed('confirm')) return void say(npc, npc.name, npc.lines[npc.said++ % npc.lines.length]);\n    // screen-relative keys become a ground direction; swings root the hero\n    const mv = inp.move(), md = game.view.screenDirToGround(mv[0], mv[1]), sp = h.sw.busy ? 20 : h.charge > .15 ? 45 : 80;\n    if (Math.hypot(md[0], md[1]) > .1 && !h.sw.busy) h.facing = Math.atan2(md[1], md[0]);\n    const hurt = h.hurt > 0, acc = (hurt ? 400 : 900) * dt; h.vx = approach(h.vx, hurt ? 0 : md[0] * sp, acc); h.vy = approach(h.vy, hurt ? 0 : md[1] * sp, acc);\n    // sword: one hit per target per swing; a press chains the combo; holding J charges, letting go spins\n    if (inp.buffered('attack') && !h.spin.busy && h.combo.press()) { inp.consume('attack'); h.charge = 0; }\n    if (inp.down('attack') && !h.sw.busy) { if (h.charge < .6 && (h.charge += dt) >= .6) { A.sfx('charge'); P.glints(...h.rig.tip(), 6); game.flash('#fff4c0', .1, .35); h.rig.kick(5); } }\n    else { if (h.charge >= .6 && h.spin.start()) game.shake(2); h.charge = 0; }\n    if (h.charge >= .6 && Math.random() < dt * 12) P.glints(...h.rig.tip(), 1, '#fff4a0', 4);\n    for (const a of [h.combo, h.spin]) if (a.update(dt) === 'active') A.sfx(a === h.combo && h.combo.step < 2 ? 'swing' : 'whoosh');\n    const sw = h.sw = h.spin.busy ? h.spin : h.combo, round = sw === h.spin || h.combo.step === 2;   // spins hit all around\n    const reach = t => E.inArc(h, h.facing, t, round ? 26 : 22, round ? Math.PI : 1.4);\n    sw.hits(foes, f => f.hp > 0 && reach(f), f => strike(f, sw === h.spin ? 1.5 : 1));\n    // bushes and pots break (pots hide a gem)\n    sw.hits(things, t => t.cut && reach(t), t => {\n      t.dead = true; P.bits(t.x, t.y, 6, 14, t.cut); poof(t.x, t.y, 0, .6); A.sfx(t.prop === 'pot' ? 'bump' : 'whoosh');\n      const kind = t.drop || E.chance(.5) && (E.chance(.7) ? 'gem' : 'heart'); if (kind) items.push({ kind, x: t.x, y: t.y });\n    });\n    h.update(dt, map); settle(h);\n    // a cleared ruin reveals the key chest\n    const chest = things.find(t => t.tag === 'chest'), gate = things.find(t => t.tag === 'gate');\n    if (chest.hidden && foes.every(f => f.room !== 1 || f.dead)) { chest.hidden = false; poof(chest.x, chest.y, 0, 1.3); P.glints(chest.x, chest.y, 10, 8); A.sfx('secret'); }\n    if (!chest.hidden && !chest.open && E.dist(h, chest) < 15) {\n      chest.open = true; keys++; held = { spr: KEYS[1], t: 1.6 }; A.sfx('key'); P.glints(h.x, h.y, 40, 10); game.flash('#fff4c0', .15, .5);\n      game.after(1.6, () => say(h, 'HERO', 'I got the SHRINE KEY! Now the great door in the ruins will open.'));\n    }\n    // the key opens the door and warps the hero inside\n    if (keys > 0 && !gate.open && E.dist(h, gate) < 22) {\n      gate.open = true; keys--; A.sfx('door'); game.shake(3); P.dust(gate.x, gate.y + 10, 2, 14, { color: '#8a7a6a', speed: 50 });\n      game.after(.5, () => { Object.assign(h, { x: entry.x, y: entry.y, vx: 0, vy: 0, facing: -Math.PI / 2 }); game.cam.snap = true; game.flash('#07040c', .5); A.sfx('warp'); });\n    }\n    for (const it of items) if (!it.got && it.kind === 'relic' && Math.random() < dt * 5) P.glints(it.x, it.y, 22, 1, '#bff8ff', 14);   // the relic sparkles\n    for (const it of items) if (!it.got && E.dist(it, h) < (it.kind === 'relic' ? 15 : 10)) {\n      it.got = true; P.glints(it.x, it.y, 6, 4); if (it.kind === 'gem') { gems++; A.sfx('coin'); } else if (it.kind === 'heart') { h.hp = Math.min(h.max, h.hp + 1); A.sfx('heal'); }\n      else { won = true; held = { spr: CRYSTALS[1], t: 99 }; game.flash('#ffffff', .2); P.glints(it.x, it.y, 20, 24, '#bff8ff', 30); A.music('victory'); game.after(6, () => game.go('title')); }\n    }\n    // enemies act only in the hero's room. A hit stuns (no AI); the last plays the death, then vanish()\n    for (const f of foes) {\n      if (f.dead) continue; f.flash -= dt; f.t -= dt; f.stun -= dt; f.wake += dt;\n      const on = f.room === room, dx = h.x - f.x, dy = h.y - f.y, dd = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1;\n      if (f.dying > 0) { if ((f.dying -= dt) <= 0) vanish(f); }\n      else if (f.stun > 0) { /* flinch: knocked back */ }\n      else if (f.kind === 'rabite') {   // hops about; near the hero it crouches and shivers (the tell), POUNCES\n        if (on && f.onGround && f.t <= 0) {\n          const chase = dd < 72 || f.tell, a = chase ? Math.atan2(dy, dx) : E.dist(f, f.home) > 20 ? E.angleTo(f, f.home) : Math.random() * TAU;\n          if (dd < 34 && !f.tell) { f.tell = true; f.t = .5; }\n          else { const v = f.tell ? 210 : chase ? 75 : 35; f.push(Math.cos(a) * v, Math.sin(a) * v, 0); f.jump(chase ? 150 : 110); f.look.kick(f.tell ? 7 : 4);\n            f.t = f.tell ? 1.2 : chase ? .6 + Math.random() * .6 : .8 + Math.random(); f.tell = false; }\n        }\n      } else if (f.kind === 'bat') {   // roosts, weaves overhead, rears up (the tell), SWOOPS\n        if (f.hang) { if (on && dd < 64) { f.hang = false; f.wake = 0; f.look.kick(8); A.sfx('whoosh', { pitch: 1.8 }); } }   // woken\n        else {\n          if (on && f.swoop <= 0 && f.t <= 0 && dd < 48) { f.swoop = 1.1; f.t = 2.6; A.sfx('whoosh', { pitch: 1.6 }); }\n          f.swoop -= dt; const rear = f.swoop > .75, dive = f.swoop > 0 && !rear, acc = (dive ? 500 : 260) * dt;\n          const a = Math.atan2(dy, dx) + (f.swoop > 0 ? 0 : Math.sin(game.time * 4 + f.y) * 1.1), s = !on || rear ? 0 : dive ? 90 : 30;\n          f.vx = approach(f.vx, Math.cos(a) * s, acc); f.vy = approach(f.vy, Math.sin(a) * s, acc);\n          f.onGround = false; f.vz = ((rear ? f.fly + 14 : dive ? 5 : f.fly + Math.sin(game.time * 3 + f.x) * 3) - f.z) * (rear ? 8 : 5);\n        }\n      } else if (f.kind === 'goblin') {   // winds up (crouch, lean back, shiver, glint: the TELL), CLAWS or SLAMS\n        const busy = f.atk.busy, go = on && !busy && dd > 17 ? 32 : 0; if (!busy) f.face = Math.atan2(dy, dx);\n        f.vx = approach(f.vx, dx / dd * go, 300 * dt); f.vy = approach(f.vy, dy / dd * go, 300 * dt);\n        if (on && !busy && dd < 21 && f.t <= 0) { f.atk = E.pick(f.moves); f.atk.start(); f.look.kick(-4); f.t = 1.4; P.glints(...f.look.head(), 2, '#ffe070', 3); }\n        const ph = f.atk.update(dt); if (ph === 'active') A.sfx('swing', { pitch: .75 });\n        if (ph === 'recover' && f.atk.spec.name === 'twohand') { const [x, y] = f.look.hand(); P.dust(x, y, 0, 10); game.shake(2); A.sfx('stomp'); }   // the slam lands\n        f.atk.hits([h], t => E.inArc(f, f.face, t, 21, 1.3), () => hurtHero(f.face));\n      } else if (on) {   // mage: sidesteps, AIMS (the cast's end pose backwards), CASTS (a ring grows), fires as the staff points\n        const c = f.atk; f.face = Math.atan2(dy, dx);\n        if (c.update(dt) === 'recover') { const [x, y, z] = f.look.hand(), [vx, vy] = E.pattern.aim({ x, y }, h, 100); shots.fire({ x, y, z, vx, vy, r: 3, team: 'foe', color: '#e060ff', core: '#ffe8ff' }); P.glints(x, y, z, 5, '#ff80e0', 8); P.glints(f.x, f.y, 2, 10, '#ff80e0', 14); A.sfx('laser', { pitch: .8 }); }\n        f.aim = !c.busy && f.t < .6 && E.move('cast', Math.max(0, f.t / .6), 'recover');\n        if (!c.busy && f.t <= 0) { c.start(); f.t = 2.4; A.sfx('charge', { pitch: 1.5, vol: .06 }); }\n        if (c.busy || f.aim) f.vx = f.vy = 0;   // planted\n        else { const s = Math.sin(game.time * .9 + f.x) > 0 ? 22 : -22; f.vx = -dy / dd * s; f.vy = dx / dd * s; }\n      }\n      if (!f.hang) f.update(dt, map); if (!f.fly) settle(f);\n      const dead = f.dying > 0, air = !f.onGround && !f.fly;\n      // Blob: squash, stretch, squash on landing; a woken bat drops, flips, unfurls; wings beat fast to rear, fold to dive; the dead flip belly-up\n      if (f.look instanceof E.Blob) { if (f.landed) f.look.kick(dead ? -9 : -4);\n        f.look.update(dt, { squash: dead ? -.4 : f.tell ? -.42 + shiver(.05) : air ? clamp(f.vz / 600, -.2, .25) : f.fly ? Math.sin(game.time * 14) * .06 : f.t < .12 ? -.18 : 0,\n          look: [dx, dy], walk: air ? 1 : 0, squint: dead || f.stun > 0, hang: f.hang || f.wake < .15 || dead && f.dying < .55, flap: f.hang || dead ? 0 : clamp((f.wake - .15) * 2.5, 0, 1) * (f.swoop > .75 ? 1.6 : f.swoop > 0 ? 0 : 1) }); }\n      else f.look.update(dt, { x: f.x, y: f.y, z: f.z, vx: f.vx, vy: f.vy, facing: f.face, hurt: f.stun > 0, attack: f.atk.state || f.aim || null,\n        pose: dead ? 'die' : null, expr: f.kind === 'goblin' && 'angry' });   // death: stagger, the knees give, topple\n      // contact on first touch (mid-pounce too; a diving bat where it meets him ON SCREEN, sooner from behind), then bounce off\n      const behind = Math.max(0, dx * game.view.fx + dy * game.view.fy), reach = f.fly ? (f.swoop > 0 && f.swoop < .75 ? 10 + behind * .65 : f.z < 9 ? 10 : 0) : f.r + h.r;\n      if (on && !dead && f.kind !== 'goblin' && dd < reach && hurtHero(Math.atan2(dy, dx))) { f.vx = f.vy = f.swoop = 0; E.knockback(h, f, 90); }\n    }\n    shots.update(dt, map); shots.hit([h], b => hurtHero(Math.atan2(b.vy, b.vx)), 'foe');\n    for (const c of pets) {   // the cat strolls and dozes\n      if ((c.t -= dt) <= 0) { const a = E.dist(c, c.home) > 18 ? E.angleTo(c, c.home) : E.rand(0, TAU), go = E.chance(.6); c.t = go ? 1.2 : E.rand(2, 4); const v = go ? 22 : 0; c.vx = Math.cos(a) * v; c.vy = Math.sin(a) * v; }\n      c.update(dt, map); settle(c); const walk = Math.min(1, Math.hypot(c.vx, c.vy) / 20);\n      c.look.update(dt, { look: walk ? [c.vx, c.vy] : [h.x - c.x, h.y - c.y], walk, squint: !walk && E.dist(c, h) > 50, squash: walk ? 0 : .12 });\n    }\n    // ambient life: petals, fireflies, embers, smoke, fountain spray, river foam\n    const rx = (room + Math.random()) * ROOM[0], ry = OY + E.rand(T, ROOM[1] - T);\n    if (Math.random() < dt * 4) P.add(room === 0 ? { kind: 'bit', x: rx, y: ry, z: 50, vx: 14, vy: 5, vz: -9, g: 3, max: 5, color: E.pick(['#ffb0c8', '#fff0f4']) }\n      : room === 1 ? { kind: 'ember', x: rx, y: ry, z: E.rand(6, 26), vx: E.rand(-5, 5), vy: E.rand(-5, 5), vz: 3, max: 2.5, color: '#d8ff6a' }\n      : { kind: 'ember', x: rx, y: ry, z: 2, vz: 16, vx: E.rand(-4, 4), max: 2, color: '#ff8a3a' });\n    for (const f of roofs) if (roomOf(f.x1) === room && Math.random() < dt * 2.5) P.smoke(f.x1 - 12, f.y0 + 14, f.h + 16, 1, { size: 2.2, color: '#e4e2ee', dark: '#b0acc0', light: '#ffffff' });\n    for (const t of things) if (t.tag === 'fountain' && t.room === room && Math.random() < dt * 14) P.add({ kind: 'bit', x: t.x, y: t.y, z: 22, vx: E.rand(-15, 15), vy: E.rand(-6, 6), vz: 40, g: 260, max: .5, color: E.pick(['#ffffff', '#a8e0ff']) });\n    if (room === 0 && Math.random() < dt * 6) P.add({ kind: 'bit', x: E.rand(11.3, 12.7) * T, y: OY + E.pick([2, 8]) * T + E.rand(0, 46), z: 0, vy: 26, max: 1.2, color: '#d8f0ff' });\n    poseHero(dt); game.focus(h.x, h.y, 10);\n    const rooms = game.settings.advCamera !== 'scroll' && game.zoom <= 1 && !game.yaw;   // zoomed or turned: it follows the hero\n    game.cam.room = rooms ? ROOM : null; game.cam.smooth = rooms ? .18 : .12;\n  }\n\n  /* ---- DRAWING ---- */\n  // POOF: five crisp puffs, aged by game.time (hit-stop holds it)\n  const poof = (x, y, z, s) => fx.push({ x, y, z: z + 4 * s, s, t: game.time, life: .5 });\n  function drawFx(r) {\n    E.prune(fx, f => game.time - f.t > f.life);\n    for (const f of fx) r.queue(f.x, f.y, f.z, g => {\n      const u = (game.time - f.t) / f.life, [x, y] = r.w(f.x, f.y, f.z), R = f.s * (u < .25 ? 3 + u * 16 : 7 - (u - .25) * 6);\n      for (const [c, k, o, d] of [['#4a3a5a', .62, 1, 0], ['#ffffff', .62, 0, 0], ['#d8d0ec', .32, 0, 1.5]])\n        for (const [dx, dy] of [[0, 0], [-1, -.6], [1, -.6], [-.7, .5], [.7, .5]]) px.disc(g, x + dx * R * .8 + d, y + dy * R * .6 - u * 6 + d, R * k + o, c);\n    }, { bias: .6 });\n  }\n  // BUSHES of LEAF CLUMPS, no two alike: one outline around the mass, a body and lit top per clump, leaf dots, blossoms\n  function bush(g, x, y, s, C, k) {\n    const H = i => E.hash2(k, i), n = 4 + Math.floor(H(0) * 4), cl = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const a = H(i + 9) - .5, b = H(i + 19); cl.push([x + a * (8 + H(1) * 12) * s, y - (3 + b * 4 + (.5 - Math.abs(a)) * 8) * s, (3 + b * 2) * s]); }\n    for (const [X, Y, R] of cl) px.disc(g, X, Y, R + 1, C[0]);\n    for (const [X, Y, R] of cl) { px.disc(g, X, Y, R, C[1]); px.disc(g, X - R * .3, Y - R * .35, R * .6, C[2]); }\n    for (let i = 0; i < n * 3; i++) { const [X, Y, R] = cl[i % n]; px.dot(g, X + (H(i + 29) - .6) * R * 1.5, Y + (H(i + 59) - .7) * R * 1.4, H(2) < .3 && i % 3 < 1 ? '#ffc8dc' : C[3 + i % 2]); }\n  }\n  // PITCHED ROOF: a shaded back half and a ridge cap read as two slopes; an eave lip and shadow; a chimney of r.box\n  function roof(r, f) {\n    const P = r.w.bind(r), m = (f.y0 + f.y1) / 2 - 1, z = f.h + .3, C = f.C, band = (x0, x1, y0, y1, z0, z1) => [P(x0, y0, z0), P(x1, y0, z0), P(x1, y1, z1), P(x0, y1, z1)];\n    r.queue(f.x1 - 1, f.y1 - 1, f.h, g => {\n      px.blend(g, .32, 'multiply', () => px.poly(g, band(f.x0, f.x1, f.y0, m, z, z), '#4a3a7a'));\n      px.blend(g, .4, 'multiply', () => px.poly(g, band(f.x0, f.x1, f.y1 + .1, f.y1 + .1, f.h - 2, f.h - 7), '#3a2a5a'));\n      px.poly(g, band(f.x0 - 1.5, f.x1 + 1.5, f.y1 - 1, f.y1 + 1.5, z, f.h - 1.5), C[0]);   // eave lip\n      px.poly(g, band(f.x0 - 1, f.x1 + 1, m - 1.5, m + 1.5, z + .8, z + .8), C[1]);   // ridge cap\n      px.line(g, ...P(f.x0 - 1, m - 1.5, z + .8), ...P(f.x1 + 1, m - 1.5, z + .8), C[4]);\n      const cx = f.x1 - 12, cy = f.y0 + 14;\n      r.box(g, cx - 3, cy - 3, f.h - 4, cx + 3, cy + 3, f.h + 11, '#6a3430', '#b05a48');\n      r.box(g, cx - 4, cy - 4, f.h + 10, cx + 4, cy + 4, f.h + 12, '#b8a8a0', '#6a5a60');\n      r.box(g, cx - 1.5, cy - 2, f.h + 12, cx + 1.5, cy + 1, f.h + 12.3, '#2a1c20', '#2a1c20');\n    }, { bias: .01 });\n  }\n  // LIGHT SHAFTS: tinted beams, a stepped FALLOFF (three additive layers), drifting motes; none in topdown\n  function shafts(r, room) {\n    const [xs, c, lean] = BEAMS[room], t = game.real;\n    if (r.view.pitchDeg < 70) r.overlay(g => { for (const bx of xs) {\n      const [x, y] = r.w(room * ROOM[0] + bx, OY + 12, 40), w = 5 + Math.sin(t * .5 + bx) * 1.5, L = 120;\n      px.blend(g, 1 / 8, 'add', () => { for (const k of [1, .6, .3]) { const X = x + lean * k, Y = y + L * k, s = w * (1 + k); px.poly(g, [[x - w, y], [x + w, y], [X + s, Y], [X - s, Y]], c); } });\n      px.blend(g, 1, 'add', () => { for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) { const u = (i * .17 + t * .025 + bx * .01) % 1; px.dot(g, x + lean * u + Math.sin(t * .7 + i * 2) * w, y + L * u, c); } });\n    } });\n  }\n  function draw(r) {\n    const view = E.charView(r.view), h = hero, room = roomOf(h.x), bob = Math.sin(game.time * 4) * 1.5;   // view: rigs get a sprite-like angle\n    bg.draw(r); map.drawFloor(r); map.queueWalls(r);\n    for (const b of [h, ...npcs, ...foes, ...pets]) if (!b.dead) shadow(r, b.x, b.y, (b.look instanceof E.Blob ? 5 : 6) - Math.min(2.5, (b.z || 0) * .12));\n    for (const f of roofs) roof(r, f);\n    for (const t of things) {\n      if (t.dead || t.hidden) continue; const y = t.face ? t.y + T / 2 + 1 : t.y, z = t.face ? t.z || 0 : map.heightAt(t.x, t.y);\n      if (t.r && !t.shape) shadow(r, t.x, t.y + 1, t.r);   // (a shape casts its own)\n      if (t.prop === 'bush') r.queue(t.x, t.y, z, g => { const [X, Y] = r.w(t.x, t.y, z), k = Math.floor(t.x * 3 + t.y);\n        bush(g, Math.round(X), Math.round(Y), t.size || 1, t.C || (t.C = E.ramp(t.color || ['#4a9a4a', '#3a8a52', '#5a9a3a'][k % 3], 5, 1.2)), k); });\n      else if (t.shape) r.shape(t.shape, t.x, y, z, { scale: t.size, facing: E.hash2(t.x, t.y) * E.TAU });   // each turned its own way\n      else r.prop(t.prop, t.x, y, z, { ...t, light: false });   // its fields style the prop\n      // GPU lights in the hero's room only; wall lights cast shadows\n      if (t.light && t.room === room) L.add(t.x, y + (t.prop === 'window' ? 30 : 0), z + 14, t.face ? 90 : 60, .9, { color: t.light, shadow: t.face });\n    }\n    for (const it of items) if (!it.got) {\n      if (it.kind === 'relic') r.sprite(it.x, it.y, 18 + bob, CRYSTALS[0], { glow: .5 });   // (its sparkle comes from update: draw changes nothing)\n      else { shadow(r, it.x, it.y, 3); r.sprite(it.x, it.y, 3 + bob, it.kind === 'gem' ? GEM : HEART, { glow: .5 }); }\n    }\n    for (const b of [...npcs, ...pets]) r.actor(b.x, b.y, b.z || 0, (g, ox, oy) => (b.rig || b.look).draw(g, ox, oy, view), { every: 2, key: b });   // townsfolk animate every other frame (a phone's frame time goes to the hero and foes)\n    for (const f of foes) if (!f.dead) {   // tells shiver (a goblin's builds); dying foes blink before the poof\n      const c = f.atk, tell = f.tell ? .7 : f.kind === 'goblin' && c.phase === 'wind' ? .3 + c.u * 1.5 : 0;\n      r.actor(f.x + shiver(tell), f.y, f.z, (g, ox, oy) => f.look.draw(g, ox, oy, view), { flash: f.flash > 0 || f.dying > 0 && f.dying < .4 && Math.floor(game.time * 16) % 2 });\n      if (f.kind === 'goblin') f.look.drawSmear(r, ['#ffffff', '#fff0d0', '#ffc890', '#e08048']);\n      // the mage's rune ring grows through the wind-up and BURSTS outward as the bolt leaves\n      const R = f.kind !== 'mage' ? 0 : c.phase === 'wind' ? 4 + c.u * 8 : c.phase === 'active' ? 12 : c.phase && c.u < .3 ? 12 + c.u * 40 : 0;\n      if (R) r.decal(() => r.groundRing(f.x, f.y, R, R > 12 ? '#ffe8ff' : '#ff70d8'), { emissive: 1 });\n      const age = game.time - f.hitT, top = (f.look.head ? f.look.head()[2] + 8 : f.z + 20) + 8 * Math.sqrt(age);   // the damage number rides its foe\n      if (age < .8) r.queue(f.x, f.y, top, g => { const [x, y] = r.w(f.x, f.y, top); txt(g, String(f.dmg), x, y, '#fff2c4', { align: 'center' }); }, { bias: 2 });\n    }\n    // the HERO: the sword trail sorts in front, so while the blade is behind him (or spinning) bias draws him over it\n    const st = h.sw.state, [tx, ty] = h.rig.tip(), over = st && (st.spec.spin || (tx - h.x) * r.view.fx + (ty - h.y) * r.view.fy < 0);\n    if (h.hp > 0 && !(h.inv > 0 && h.hurt <= 0 && Math.floor(game.real * 15) % 2)) {\n      r.actor(h.x + shiver(h.charge * .6), h.y, h.z, (g, ox, oy) => {\n        h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view);\n        if (held && held.t > 0) {   // the prize, placed through the character view\n          const s = held.spr, q = view.p(0, 0, h.rig.head()[2] - h.z + 9 + bob * .5);\n          px.glow(g, .35); px.sprite(g, s, Math.round(ox + q[0] - s.w / 2), Math.round(oy + q[1] - s.h));\n        }\n      }, { xray: true, flash: h.hurt > .15 || h.charge >= .6 && game.time % .3 < .05, bias: over ? 2 : 0 });\n      h.rig.drawSmear(r);\n    }\n    shots.draw(r); drawFx(r); shafts(r, room); if (game.cam.room) curtain(r, room); hud(r); talk.draw(r);\n  }\n  // the CURTAIN: what the screen shows beyond the hero's room, dimmed a little (the room's box: its floor, its walls' height)\n  function curtain(r, room) {\n    let x0 = 1e9, y0 = 1e9, x1 = -1e9, y1 = -1e9;\n    for (const x of [room * ROOM[0], (room + 1) * ROOM[0]]) for (const y of [OY, OY + ROOM[1]]) for (const z of [0, 48]) { const [sx, sy] = r.w(x, y, z); x0 = Math.min(x0, sx); x1 = Math.max(x1, sx); y0 = Math.min(y0, sy); y1 = Math.max(y1, sy); }\n    [x0, y0, x1, y1] = [x0, y0, x1, y1].map(Math.round);\n    if (x0 <= 0 && y0 <= 0 && x1 >= r.W && y1 >= r.H) return;\n    r.overlay(g => px.blend(g, .4, 'normal', () => { const D = '#0a0818'; px.rect(g, 0, 0, r.W, y0, D); px.rect(g, 0, y1, r.W, r.H - y1, D); px.rect(g, 0, y0, x0, y1 - y0, D); px.rect(g, x1, y0, r.W - x1, y1 - y0, D); }));\n  }\n  // HUD in the corners, over the world: the hero and his hearts top left; gems, keys and a map of the rooms top right\n  // (clear of the corner's buttons); the CONTROLS (the player's own keys) bottom right, not on a touch screen (its buttons\n  // say it); the area's name drops in under them as he enters\n  function hud(r) {\n    const npc = talkable(), R = Math.min(r.W, cornerX()) - 4;\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      E.ui.box(g, 4, 4, 84, 30, WIN); hero.rig.drawPortrait(g, 9, 9, 20, { zoom: 1.5, cape: false, bg: FACE_BG });\n      txt(g, 'HERO', 36, 8, '#ffe08a', { gradient: ['#fff4c0', '#e8a040'] }); E.ui.hearts(g, 36, 19, hero.hp, hero.max);\n      const GX = R - 70; E.ui.box(g, GX, 4, 70, 17, WIN); px.sprite(g, GEM, GX + 6, 9); px.sprite(g, KEYS[0], GX + 41, 10);\n      txt(g, String(gems).padStart(3, '0'), GX + 14, 9, '#ffffff'); txt(g, 'x' + keys, GX + 50, 9, '#ffffff');\n      minimap(g, GX, 24);\n      if (won) {\n        const wy = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 24;\n        E.ui.box(g, r.W / 2 - 90, wy, 180, 48, WIN); E.font.title(g, 'MANA CRYSTAL!', r.W / 2, wy + 7, { align: 'center', scale: 2, colors: ['#ffffff', '#bff8ff', '#4ac8e8'], depth: 1 });\n        return txt(g, 'Gems ' + gems + '    Best ' + best('adventure', gems), r.W / 2, wy + 34, '#ffe08a', { align: 'center' });\n      }\n      if (talk.open) return;\n      if (!touch()) {\n        const a = prompt('attack', 'Sword'), b = prompt('confirm', 'Talk'), w = E.font.width(a) + E.font.width(b) + 26, cx = r.W - w - 4, cy = r.H - 22;\n        E.ui.box(g, cx, cy, w, 18, WIN); txt(g, a, cx + 8, cy + 5, '#d8d0f0');\n        txt(g, b, cx + w - 8 - E.font.width(b), cy + 5, npc && Math.floor(game.real * 3) % 2 ? '#ffe08a' : '#d8d0f0');   // 'Talk' blinks near a villager\n      }\n      if (npc) {   // a speech bubble: you can talk\n        const [fx, fy] = r.w(npc.x, npc.y, 0), q = E.charView(r.view).p(0, 0, 44), x = Math.round(fx + q[0]), y = Math.round(fy + q[1]);\n        E.ui.box(g, x - 11, y - 14, 22, 12, WIN); px.poly(g, [[x - 4, y - 3], [x + 2, y - 3], [x - 3, y + 1]], WIN.border);\n        for (let k = 0; k < 3; k++) px.rect(g, x - 6 + k * 5, y - 9 - (Math.floor(game.real * 3) % 3 === k ? 1 : 0), 2, 2, '#ffe08a');\n      }\n      if (area.t > 0) {   // the area's name drops in, then goes\n        const w = E.font.width(AREAS[area.room]) + 20, y = Math.round(42 - (Math.max(0, area.t - 2.3) + Math.max(0, .3 - area.t)) * 120);\n        E.ui.box(g, (r.W - w) / 2, y, w, 18, WIN); txt(g, AREAS[area.room], r.W / 2, y + 5, '#ffffff', { align: 'center' });\n      }\n    });\n  }\n  // a map of the three rooms, 70 x 12: the hero's lit, where he stands blinking\n  function minimap(g, x, y) {\n    const room = roomOf(hero.x), C = ['#4a9a4a', '#7a8a56', '#5a5486'], w = 22, h = 12;\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) { px.rect(g, x + i * (w + 2), y, w, h, i === room ? '#fff4c0' : '#1a1838'); px.rect(g, x + i * (w + 2) + 1, y + 1, w - 2, h - 2, i === room ? C[i] : E.shade(C[i], -.45)); }\n    if (Math.floor(game.real * 3) % 2) px.rect(g, x + Math.round(hero.x / ROOM[0] * (w + 2)) - 1, y + 1 + Math.round(clamp((hero.y - OY) / ROOM[1], 0, 1) * (h - 4)), 2, 2, '#ffffff');\n  }\n  return { view: 'threequarter', views: ['threequarter', 'topdown', 'iso'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1', propSize: 1.25, pausable: true, touch: ['attack', 'confirm'], enter: start, update, draw,\n    // the player zooms in to 2x, and out as far as the world round the rooms fills the screen: to .85x on a wide one, not\n    // at all held upright (its forest is sized for 1x there). A TileMap scene rotates cleanly\n    camera: { zoom: g => [g.upright ? 1 : .85, 2], rotate: true },\n    state: () => ({ hero, foes, things, items, map, npcs, pets, talk }),   // for tests\n    /** the proof: a walk round the village and into the ruins, the sword swinging and every word read; a hash of the run */\n    run: (n = 600) => proof('adventure', n, (i, k) => { walk(i, k, ['right', 'down', 'left', 'up'], 90); if (i % 40 === 20) k.tap('attack'); if (i % 120 === 60) k.tap('confirm'); },\n      () => [hero.x, hero.y, hero.hp, gems, keys, area, won, foes.map(f => [f.x, f.y, f.hp])]),\n    exit() { game.cam.room = null; game.cam.smooth = .18; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; } };\n})();\nscenes.adventure = ADV;\n\n/* ---- START: the title menu, or a slice named in the address (#platformer) ---- */\n// a genre kit file holds one slice: the menu lists only the slices in this file\nfor (let i = SLICES.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (!scenes[SLICES[i].id]) SLICES.splice(i, 1);\ntitleMenu = menuOf(SLICES, { y: 76, onPick: i => game.go(SLICES[i].id) });\n// #<slice>/<part> jumps in (#arcade/maze, #shooter/horizontal): the slice's enter(data) gets { part }; a part that is a\n// scene of its own (the slice's parts: { battle: 'rpg-battle' }) starts there\nconst [first, part] = (location.hash || '').slice(1).split('/'), sc = scenes[first], to = sc && part && sc.parts && sc.parts[part];\ngame.start({ scenes, scene: to || (sc ? first : 'title'), data: sc && part ? { part } : undefined });\nwindow.__game = { game, scenes, titleMenu };   // for tests\n})();\n/* =============================== GAME END =============================== */\n// The handoff package's template game: a rooftop thief in the isometric view. Climb onto the roof, take the gem, and\n// don't let the guard in the street watch you for long. It shows what a game is made of (scenes, a TileMap with roofs, a\n// Mover and a Humanoid, input, the camera, a HUD) and the height-aware API: E.Mover climbs any wall (climbAny: jump at\n// it, the stick climbs, jump leaps up, it pulls up at the top) and glides (glide: jump again in the air; a sail drawn\n// over it), both on its stamina, the guard is a plain Body, map.sight and E.inArc for\n// the guard's eyes (they see over the planter, not through the roof), shapes and materials (docs/ASSETS.md: barrels and\n// crates as data, solid with map.solid; the street's cobbles a material), and game.debug for tests and tools. The pause menu,\n// settings, rebinding and full screen come with every game: menu: { controls } names the actions on its Controls screen,\n// and input.label() puts the player's own key or button in a prompt. The night is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n// ambient, and lights added every draw (a street lamp, the gem's glow), the same in every browser and every check. The\n// HUD is HTML (E.Shell: the objective with its distance, the guard's alert, your keys), over the pixels; the title and\n// end screens are pixel art.\n// Copy it and make it your game. Test it headless: node game/test.mjs. Check it in a browser: node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'],   // expand: full screen at any shape (the HUD anchors to r.W, r.H)\n  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } },   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\n  draw: true });   // (headless too: game/test.mjs draws every advance on a stand-in, so a draw error shows in game.errors)\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game);   // the HTML HUD (it keeps the standard pause menu); headless, it draws nothing\nconst ROOF = 32;\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['############',\n         '#..........#',\n         '#.@........#',\n         '#....p.....#',\n         '#......RRR.#',\n         '#......RGR.#',\n         '#..s...RRR.#',\n         '#..........#',\n         '############'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, R: 2, G: { tile: 2, spawn: 'gem' }, p: 3, '@': 'hero', s: 'guard' },\n  types: { 1: { h: 48, top: '#5a5068', side: '#3e3650', cut: true },\n           2: { h: ROOF, top: '#9a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n           3: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n  floorMat: 'cobble'   // a material (E.MATERIALS, or '#hex pattern'): the floor, wall faces and tops, shapes' parts all take them\n});\n// set dressing: shapes (E.SHAPES: objects as data, right in every view), solid where they stand (map.solid: walk into one, land on it)\nconst DRESS = [['barrel', 152, 30, { facing: .5 }], ['barrel', 166, 26, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 22, 120, { facing: .3 }], ['cart', 72, 26, { facing: 0 }]];\nfor (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) map.solid(id, x, y, 0, o);\nconst GEM = E.sprite(['.c.', 'cCc', '.c.'], { c: '#48c8f0', C: '#e8faff' }, 2);\nlet hero, heroRig, guard, guardRig, alert, got, won;\n\nfunction reset() {\n  const h = map.find('hero'), g = map.find('guard');\n  hero = new E.Mover({ x: h.x, y: h.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 24, glide: true, staminaMax: 100 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (the roof, 32 high, is climbed)\n  heroRig = heroRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hood: true, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth: '#3a4a6a', cape: '#2a3a52' } });\n  guard = new E.Body({ x: g.x, y: g.y, r: 5 }); guard.facing = 0; guard.dir = 1;\n  guardRig = guardRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'sword', hat: 'helmet', colors: { cloth: '#8a3a32' } });\n  alert = 0; got = false; won = false;\n}\n\nconst title = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(['#141030', '#3a2a60']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);   // centred on any screen\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'ROOFTOP', r.W / 2, m - 52, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('CLIMB WITH ' + game.input.label('jump') + '  TAKE THE GEM  STAY UNSEEN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 8, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center' });\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start')).toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 38, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nconst play = {\n  pausable: true,\n  enter() { game.follow(hero, { z: 16 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.lights.enabled = true; game.lights.ambient = .5; },\n  exit() { game.lights.enabled = false; ui.hud({}); },\n  update(dt) {\n    const I = game.input, was = !!(hero.wall || hero.action);\n    hero.update(dt, map, I);   // walks, jumps, climbs: the stick and the jump button, through the view\n    if (!was && (hero.wall || hero.action)) game.audio.sfx('jump');\n    // the guard walks the street and watches ahead: its eyes see over the planter, not through the roof\n    guard.vx = guard.dir * 30; guard.update(dt, map);\n    if (guard.x > 112 || guard.hitWall) guard.dir = -1; else if (guard.x < 40) guard.dir = 1;\n    guard.facing = guard.dir > 0 ? 0 : Math.PI;\n    const sees = map.sight(guard, hero) && E.inArc(guard, guard.facing, hero, 110, .6);\n    alert = sees ? alert + dt : Math.max(0, alert - dt * .5);\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got && E.dist(hero, { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }) < 12) { got = true; game.audio.sfx('coin'); game.flash('#c8f4ff', .15); }\n    if (got && hero.z < 2) { won = true; game.go('end'); }   // back down in the street with it\n    else if (alert > 1.2) { won = false; game.audio.sfx('hurt'); game.go('end'); }\n    // the rigs are posed every step from the bodies' motion; draw only draws them\n    heroRig.update(dt, hero.rigState());\n    guardRig.update(dt, { x: guard.x, y: guard.y, z: guard.z, vx: guard.vx, vy: 0, facing: guard.facing, stance: 'ready' });\n    // the HUD, from this step's state (E.Shell redraws only what changed; the keys hide on a touch screen)\n    ui.hud({ objective: got ? { title: 'Bring it down', text: 'Back to the street with it' } : { title: 'Take the gem', text: hero.wall ? 'Climb: up, and jump to leap' : 'It lies on the roof', at: { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }, from: hero },\n      bars: [{ label: 'Seen', value: Math.min(alert, 1.2), max: 1.2, color: '#ff6040' }, { label: 'Stamina', value: hero.stamina, max: hero.staminaMax, color: hero.exhausted ? '#ff6040' : '#7ad06a' }],\n      keys: [[['up', 'left', 'down', 'right'].map(a => I.label(a)).join(''), 'Move'], [I.label('jump'), 'Jump, climb, glide']] });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    map.drawFloor(r); map.queueWalls(r);   // (the floor runs on past the map to the screen's edges: map.outside)\n    for (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) r.shape(id, x, y, 0, o);\n    r.prop('lamp', 88, 88, 0, { light: true });   // a street lamp: its glow and a pool of light\n    r.decal(() => r.groundArc(guard.x, guard.y, 6, 110, guard.facing - .6, guard.facing + .6, alert > 0 ? '#ff6040' : '#ffe080', .4));   // its sight cone\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got) { r.sprite(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6 + Math.sin(game.time * 3) * 2, GEM, { glow: .8 }); game.lights.add(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6, 44, .9, { color: '#80d8ff' }); }\n    if (hero.gliding) r.queue(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 40, g => {   // the sail, over the hands the rig holds up\n      const c = Math.cos(hero.facing), s = Math.sin(hero.facing), P = (f, w, z) => r.w(hero.x + c * f - s * w, hero.y + s * f + c * w, hero.z + z);\n      const q = [P(9, -17, 43), P(9, 17, 43), P(-7, 15, 37), P(-7, -15, 37)], h = P(0, 0, 30);\n      for (const t of [q[0], q[1]]) E.px.line(g, t[0], t[1], h[0], h[1], '#3a2a20');\n      E.px.poly(g, q, '#d8603a'); E.px.line(g, q[0][0], q[0][1], q[1][0], q[1][1], '#f4a070');\n    });\n    for (const [b, rig] of [[hero, heroRig], [guard, guardRig]]) {\n      r.shadow(b.x, b.y, 7, .35, undefined, b.groundZ || 0);\n      r.actor(b.x, b.y, b.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst end = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(won ? ['#103020', '#2a6a48'] : ['#301010', '#6a2a2a']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, won ? 'STOLEN' : 'CAUGHT', r.W / 2, m - 42, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start') + ' TO TRY AGAIN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 28, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nreset();\n// a handle for tests and tools (node game/test.mjs, tools/check.mjs prints snapshot(), tools/replay.mjs logs it)\ngame.debug = {\n  snapshot: () => ({ scene: game.sceneName, hero: [hero.x, hero.y, hero.z].map(v => Math.round(v * 10) / 10), climbing: !!(hero.wall || hero.action),\n    guard: [Math.round(guard.x), Math.round(guard.y), guard.facing], alert: Math.round(alert * 100) / 100, got, won }),\n  teleport(x, y, z = 0, facing = hero.facing) { Object.assign(hero, { x, y, z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, onGround: true, facing, wall: null, action: null }); }\n};\ngame.start({ scenes: { title, play, end }, scene: 'title' });\n})();\n// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
