();if(h.bag.length)equipItem(W,h,h.bag.at(-1));PANEL_STATE=null;}\n  if(vignette.zone==='town')\\\"\\\"\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('tools/test.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"host=frames.find(async()=>true),\\\",'');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode tools/test.mjs sim\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_92","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > game/CONTENT.md <<'MD'\n# Adding content to Diabellum\n\nThe game uses the full my-3D2dge v0.89.1 handoff. Runtime modules in \"'`src/` share one IIFE. `tools/build.mjs` loads `00-core.js`, every file in `src/data/` in name order, then the remaining numbered modules. The build writes `game/game.js`, a development page, the root single-file HTML and `exit-interview.json`. The title and output basename come from `build-config.json`.\n\nRun `node tools/build.mjs` to bundle. Open the resulting root HTML directly, or `game/index.html`. No server or downloaded assets are needed to play. Run `node tools/test.mjs` for the full test command; add `data`, `sim`, `play`, `browser`, or `hub` to select a suite. `browser --matrix` captures the 14 viewport matrix. `hub --quick` runs the four protocol scenarios without the extra minute-long synchronization run. All generated pictures and reports stay under `check-output/`.\n\n## Registries and the simulation\n\n`def(kind, id, spec)` registers content. Hero, skill, monster, affix, boss, zone, Relic and set definitions live in the data folder. Simulation objects have world coordinates, health, timers and IDs; they never read a visual rig. A `world` contains `heroes`, `foes`, `allies`, `corpses`, `objects`, `drops`, `hazards` and `fx`. The same world code serves solo, couch co-op, the Hub host and the headless tests. Named seeded streams separate layouts, combat and loot.\n\nTo add a skill, use the `skill()` helper in `01-heroes.js`. Pick a shared verb (`cone`, `wave`, `bolt`, `chain`, `nova`, `area`, `lob`, `bell`, `leap`, `charge`, `blink`, `buff`, `guard`, `summon`, `corpse`, `heal` or `beam`). Give it damage relative to weapon damage, range, radius, cost, cooldown and a native move. Each of its three Tones has a name, short text and modifiers. Modifiers include `mul`, `rangeMul`, `radiusMul`, `costMul`, `cdMul`, `element`, `stun`, `slow`, `burn`, `pull`, `pool`, `triple`, `chain`, `pierce`, `leech` and `ring`. Add its ID to a hero'\"'s list and unlock it there. The tests cast every skill and Tone.\n\nWorked example, a Cantor wave:\n\n\"'```js\nskill('\"'cantor', 'quietAsh', 'Quiet Ash', 'wave', 2.1, 130, 20, 20, 3, 'cast', [\n  ['Wide', 'A wider verse.', {radiusMul:1.5}],\n  ['Cold', 'The ash chills.', {element:'frost',slow:1}],\n  ['Cinder', 'The ash remembers fire.', {element:'fire',burn:1}]\n]);\n\"'```\n\nA monster definition supplies a native or custom body, AI kind, speed, life and damage multipliers, wind-up, attack range, move and death material. AI kinds are shamble, rusher, charger, kiter, support, summoner, flier, burrower and thief. `dealDamage()` is the only damage pipeline. To add an elite affix, register a timed pattern and implement its shared hazard in `applyAffix()`. Bosses list health thresholds and pattern IDs; `bossPattern()` is the common pattern library. Telegraphs and effects replicate through shared network events.\n\n## World, quests and objects\n\nA zone definition chooses a theme, dimensions, layout, enemy pool, count, kill requirement and interactive objects. Layouts are ASCII arrays with `#` stone, `H` timber houses, `.` floor and `~` blocked void; `makeRows()` generates them and preserves the main causeway. Add a hand-authored layout by returning its rows there. Vigil geometry and all dressing use seeded streams. Named themes control floor, walls, ambient light, weather and the score. Props are data objects placed from the dressing stream. Native still objects are `E.SHAPES` entries; the game'\"'s bells, headstones, gate, pew and foundry wheel are worked examples in \"'`50-art.js`.\n\n`CAMPAIGN` is the ordered quest path. A step has a zone, title, objective, spoken line and optional speaker. `objectiveReady()` enforces required kills and objects. Add interactions to `interactNearest()` and drawing to `drawObject()`. Optional events run in the world step; their rewards use the same loot pipeline. The side chapel, caravan, sluices, grave row, cursed chest, sermon and side crypt show the patterns. `ATTRACT` is an ordered list of seeded vignettes; the bot also drives followers and the full playthrough.\n\n## Items, writing, audio and tools\n\nItems have one of eight equipment slots, a rarity, affixes and optional gem, Relic or set ID. Relics declare a power ID and flavor. Implement a power in `tunedSkill()`, `dealDamage()` or the appropriate shared event. The 24 shipped Relics are examples. The Forge, Pawn, Chandlery, stash and lantern use the same inventory operations as tests. Saves are version 2, serialized without renderer or pathfinding state; `migrateSave()` upgrades older data.\n\nUse ASCII and the engine'\"'s supported glyphs. Keep most dialogue under 90 characters. Add barks, epitaphs, lore and taunts to their data arrays. \"'`say()` displays a native Dialog and schedules deterministic gibberish through a speaker profile. `SCORES` contains original interval sequences; all voices, instruments, sound and reverb are synthesized in `55-audio.js`. Music defaults to 10% through the engine bus.\n\nEvery balance knob is in `TUNING` and read at use. Dev Mode (pause menu) has cheats, spawns, travel, sliders, resets, clipboard export and overlays. Gallery cycles every skill and Tone, monsters, affixes and boss phases. Deep links: `#zone/acre`, `#boss/regent/1`, `#vigil/3`, `#gallery`, `#attract`, `#about`; `?seed=1441` fixes a campaign. `window.__diabellum` exposes the world, registries and test operations. `game.debug.snapshot()` is the small stable inspection interface.\n\nAbout/Credits and the exit interview share `data/04-about.js`. Keep that metadata and feedback accurate when changing or testing the game.\nMD'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_92","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > game/CONTENT.md <<'MD'\n# Adding content to Diabellum\n\nThe game uses the full my-3D2dge v0.89.1 handoff. Runtime modules in \"'`src/` share one IIFE. `tools/build.mjs` loads `00-core.js`, every file in `src/data/` in name order, then the remaining numbered modules. The build writes `game/game.js`, a development page, the root single-file HTML and `exit-interview.json`. The title and output basename come from `build-config.json`.\n\nRun `node tools/build.mjs` to bundle. Open the resulting root HTML directly, or `game/index.html`. No server or downloaded assets are needed to play. Run `node tools/test.mjs` for the full test command; add `data`, `sim`, `play`, `browser`, or `hub` to select a suite. `browser --matrix` captures the 14 viewport matrix. `hub --quick` runs the four protocol scenarios without the extra minute-long synchronization run. All generated pictures and reports stay under `check-output/`.\n\n## Registries and the simulation\n\n`def(kind, id, spec)` registers content. Hero, skill, monster, affix, boss, zone, Relic and set definitions live in the data folder. Simulation objects have world coordinates, health, timers and IDs; they never read a visual rig. A `world` contains `heroes`, `foes`, `allies`, `corpses`, `objects`, `drops`, `hazards` and `fx`. The same world code serves solo, couch co-op, the Hub host and the headless tests. Named seeded streams separate layouts, combat and loot.\n\nTo add a skill, use the `skill()` helper in `01-heroes.js`. Pick a shared verb (`cone`, `wave`, `bolt`, `chain`, `nova`, `area`, `lob`, `bell`, `leap`, `charge`, `blink`, `buff`, `guard`, `summon`, `corpse`, `heal` or `beam`). Give it damage relative to weapon damage, range, radius, cost, cooldown and a native move. Each of its three Tones has a name, short text and modifiers. Modifiers include `mul`, `rangeMul`, `radiusMul`, `costMul`, `cdMul`, `element`, `stun`, `slow`, `burn`, `pull`, `pool`, `triple`, `chain`, `pierce`, `leech` and `ring`. Add its ID to a hero'\"'s list and unlock it there. The tests cast every skill and Tone.\n\nWorked example, a Cantor wave:\n\n\"'```js\nskill('\"'cantor', 'quietAsh', 'Quiet Ash', 'wave', 2.1, 130, 20, 20, 3, 'cast', [\n  ['Wide', 'A wider verse.', {radiusMul:1.5}],\n  ['Cold', 'The ash chills.', {element:'frost',slow:1}],\n  ['Cinder', 'The ash remembers fire.', {element:'fire',burn:1}]\n]);\n\"'```\n\nA monster definition supplies a native or custom body, AI kind, speed, life and damage multipliers, wind-up, attack range, move and death material. AI kinds are shamble, rusher, charger, kiter, support, summoner, flier, burrower and thief. `dealDamage()` is the only damage pipeline. To add an elite affix, register a timed pattern and implement its shared hazard in `applyAffix()`. Bosses list health thresholds and pattern IDs; `bossPattern()` is the common pattern library. Telegraphs and effects replicate through shared network events.\n\n## World, quests and objects\n\nA zone definition chooses a theme, dimensions, layout, enemy pool, count, kill requirement and interactive objects. Layouts are ASCII arrays with `#` stone, `H` timber houses, `.` floor and `~` blocked void; `makeRows()` generates them and preserves the main causeway. Add a hand-authored layout by returning its rows there. Vigil geometry and all dressing use seeded streams. Named themes control floor, walls, ambient light, weather and the score. Props are data objects placed from the dressing stream. Native still objects are `E.SHAPES` entries; the game'\"'s bells, headstones, gate, pew and foundry wheel are worked examples in \"'`50-art.js`.\n\n`CAMPAIGN` is the ordered quest path. A step has a zone, title, objective, spoken line and optional speaker. `objectiveReady()` enforces required kills and objects. Add interactions to `interactNearest()` and drawing to `drawObject()`. Optional events run in the world step; their rewards use the same loot pipeline. The side chapel, caravan, sluices, grave row, cursed chest, sermon and side crypt show the patterns. `ATTRACT` is an ordered list of seeded vignettes; the bot also drives followers and the full playthrough.\n\n## Items, writing, audio and tools\n\nItems have one of eight equipment slots, a rarity, affixes and optional gem, Relic or set ID. Relics declare a power ID and flavor. Implement a power in `tunedSkill()`, `dealDamage()` or the appropriate shared event. The 24 shipped Relics are examples. The Forge, Pawn, Chandlery, stash and lantern use the same inventory operations as tests. Saves are version 2, serialized without renderer or pathfinding state; `migrateSave()` upgrades older data.\n\nUse ASCII and the engine'\"'s supported glyphs. Keep most dialogue under 90 characters. Add barks, epitaphs, lore and taunts to their data arrays. \"'`say()` displays a native Dialog and schedules deterministic gibberish through a speaker profile. `SCORES` contains original interval sequences; all voices, instruments, sound and reverb are synthesized in `55-audio.js`. Music defaults to 10% through the engine bus.\n\nEvery balance knob is in `TUNING` and read at use. Dev Mode (pause menu) has cheats, spawns, travel, sliders, resets, clipboard export and overlays. Gallery cycles every skill and Tone, monsters, affixes and boss phases. Deep links: `#zone/acre`, `#boss/regent/1`, `#vigil/3`, `#gallery`, `#attract`, `#about`; `?seed=1441` fixes a campaign. `window.__diabellum` exposes the world, registries and test operations. `game.debug.snapshot()` is the small stable inspection interface.\n\nAbout/Credits and the exit interview share `data/04-about.js`. Keep that metadata and feedback accurate when changing or testing the game.\nMD'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
