{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_104","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('package.json');s=json.loads(p.read_text());s['name']='diabellum';s['version']='1.0.0';s['description']='An original gothic co-op action RPG';s['scripts']={'build':'node tools/build.mjs','test':'node tools/test.mjs','test:quick':'node tools/test.mjs data','check':'node tools/test.mjs browser --matrix'};p.write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('game/src/data/04-about.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"testingFeedback:['unknown','unknown','The complete campaign bot, including the final held interaction and a Vigil clear.','unknown']\\\", \\\"testingFeedback:['Testing caught 8 confirmed game defects; all were fixed.','Three could block gameplay: the town exit, input-hook signature and a summoned archer projectile source.','The complete campaign bot for all four heroes, including the final held interaction and a Vigil clear.','Static title screenshots exposed fewer consequential defects than the state-driven playthrough.']\\\");p.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode tools/test.mjs play\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_104","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('package.json');s=json.loads(p.read_text());s['name']='diabellum';s['version']='1.0.0';s['description']='An original gothic co-op action RPG';s['scripts']={'build':'node tools/build.mjs','test':'node tools/test.mjs','test:quick':'node tools/test.mjs data','check':'node tools/test.mjs browser --matrix'};p.write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('game/src/data/04-about.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"testingFeedback:['unknown','unknown','The complete campaign bot, including the final held interaction and a Vigil clear.','unknown']\\\", \\\"testingFeedback:['Testing caught 8 confirmed game defects; all were fixed.','Three could block gameplay: the town exit, input-hook signature and a summoned archer projectile source.','The complete campaign bot for all four heroes, including the final held interaction and a Vigil clear.','Static title screenshots exposed fewer consequential defects than the state-driven playthrough.']\\\");p.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode tools/test.mjs play\"","aggregated_output":"22 checks: 22 passed, 0 failed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('game/src/90-start.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"prologue:{enter(){prologuePage=0;\\\", \\\"prologue:{enter(){prologuePage=0;frontFocus=0;\\\");p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'MD'\n# Diabellum\n\nEvery soul counted. Except yours.\n\nAn original gothic action RPG built from \"'`PLAN.md` on my-3D2dge v0.89.1. The single HTML file in the parent folder plays offline: open it directly in a browser. No server, account or asset download is needed.\n\nChoose one of four parishioners. Carry Mother Quillon through three chapters, collect the iron Tongue, recast the Bell and face the Angelus. The Long Vigil offers seeded dungeons, composed Wardens, tiers, Greater Vigils and records. There are 32 skills, 96 Tones, Vows, 24 Relics, four equipment sets, gems, town services, followers and a secret field.\n\nThe campaign is a condensed complete demo. It includes its ending. Optional motion-capture clips and WebGPU lighting are omitted; the native canvas lighting remains available everywhere. All art, music, sound and gibberish voices are generated by code. Music defaults to 10%.\n\n## Controls\n\n| Action | Keyboard / mouse | Standard controller |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move | WASD, arrows, or hold click on ground | Left stick |\n| Primary / skill 2 | Click / right click, or F / G | Cross / Square |\n| Skills 3-6 | 1, 2, 3, 4 | Triangle, Circle, R1, R2 |\n| Evade | Space | Right stick flick or R3 |\n| Potion / interact | Q / E | L1 / L2 |\n| Town portal | T | D-pad up |\n| Map / bag / skills | M or Tab / I or C / K | D-pad down / left / right |\n| Journal / pause | J / Esc | Create / Options |\n\nHold Shift to stand and attack. Hold Interact to revive an ally or strike the final bell. Consecrate unknown items in the bag, then equip them. L1/R1 or bracket keys change panel tabs; arrows, Enter, Escape, hover and clicks navigate the same screens. Settings includes Xbox glyphs. Touch-only devices show a controller/keyboard notice and can watch the attract reel.\n\nA second controller joins with Options, up to four players sharing one screen. In an AI Hub session the game opens directly into a shared-world Vigil for 1-4 networked players. All network communication uses the unmodified AI Hub session client.\n\n## Development\n\n`npm install` uses the pinned Playwright version and the machine'\"'s installed browsers. \"'`npm run build` produces the root HTML and `exit-interview.json`. `npm test` is the single full test command. Select a suite with `node tools/test.mjs data`, `sim`, `play`, `browser` or `hub`. `browser --matrix` adds the 14 viewport matrix; `hub --quick` omits only the extra real-minute synchronization run.\n\nDev Mode is in the pause menu. It offers live balance sliders and resets, cheats, monster/item/boss spawns, travel, overlays and a living Gallery. See `game/CONTENT.md` for adding content. Useful links are `#zone/nave`, `#boss/regent/1`, `#vigil/3`, `#gallery/skill/knell/2`, `#gallery/boss/angelus/2`, `#attract`, `#about` and `?seed=1441`.\n\n`PROGRESS.md` in the parent folder records the build and verification. The About screen and the machine-readable interview share the metadata in `game/src/data/04-about.js`.\nMD\ncat > game/CONTENT.md <<'\"'MD'\n# Content guide\n\nBuild with \"'`node tools/build.mjs`; test with `node tools/test.mjs`. The build reads `build-config.json`, joins `00-core.js`, the sorted `src/data/*.js`, then the other numbered runtime modules into one IIFE. It writes the development page, root HTML and exit interview. The root HTML runs offline.\n\n## Registries\n\n`def(kind, id, spec)` registers heroes, skills, monsters, affixes, bosses, zones, Relics and sets. Add content in `src/data/`. Simulation never reads visual rigs. Each world owns its heroes, enemies, allies, corpses, loot, hazards and effects. Separate seeded streams drive geometry, AI, dressing and loot.\n\nSkills combine shared verbs: cone, wave, bolt, chain, nova, area, lob, bell, leap, charge, blink, buff, guard, summon, corpse, heal and beam. The `skill()` helper takes the hero, ID, name, verb, weapon-damage multiplier, range, radius, cost, cooldown, native animation and three Tones. Tone modifiers include damage, range, radius, cost and cooldown multipliers; element, stun, slow, burn, pull, pool, triple, chain, pierce, leech and Ringing. Add the ID to its hero'\"'s list. Tests cast every skill and Tone.\n\n\"'```js\nskill('\"'cantor','quietAsh','Quiet Ash','wave',2.1,130,20,20,3,'cast',[\n  ['Wide','A wider verse.',{radiusMul:1.5}],\n  ['Cold','The ash chills.',{element:'frost',slow:1}],\n  ['Cinder','The ash remembers fire.',{element:'fire',burn:1}]\n]);\n\"'```\n\nA monster supplies its body, AI kind, movement, health/damage multipliers, wind-up, reach, move and death material. Native Humanoid/Blob and custom crawler, serpent, hound and moth bodies are available. Add elite patterns in `applyAffix()`. Boss data lists health thresholds and pattern IDs; `bossPattern()` is the shared library. `dealDamage()` is the only damage pipeline. Shared hazards and effect verbs carry network events, so content needs no separate per-skill networking.\n\n## World and progression\n\nA zone chooses a theme, dimensions, layout, enemy pool/count, kill requirement and interactive objects. ASCII legend: `#` stone, `H` houses, `.` floor, `~` blocked void. Add a hand-authored layout in `makeRows()`, or use its seeded hall/island/yard generators. Preserve a walkable route between the spawn, objectives and exit. Themes control ground, walls, ambient light, weather and score. Props are seeded data; native objects use `E.SHAPES`. Bells, the gate, headstone, pew and foundry wheel in `50-art.js` are original worked examples.\n\n`CAMPAIGN` orders the quest path. Each step names a zone, title, objective, line and optional speaker. `objectiveReady()` enforces requirements. New objects need an interaction in `interactNearest()` and drawing in `drawObject()`. Existing chapels, sluices, caravan, grave row, cursed chest, sermon and side crypt demonstrate events and rewards. `ATTRACT` orders the throwaway demo vignettes. The same bot drives it, followers and the campaign test.\n\nItems have eight possible slots, rarity, affixes and optional gem, Relic or set ID. A Relic declares a power and flavor; implement its modifier in `tunedSkill()`, the damage pipeline or its shared event. Town services call the same inventory operations as tests. Saves are version 2; `serializeWorld()` omits renderer/pathfinding state and `migrateSave()` upgrades older data.\n\n## Presentation and tools\n\nUse ASCII and supported engine glyphs; keep most spoken lines under 90 characters. Add barks, lore, epitaphs and taunts to their arrays. `say()` uses native Dialog portraits and deterministic gibberish profiles. `SCORES` holds original interval sequences; instruments, reverb, voices and effects are synthesized in `55-audio.js`.\n\nAll balance controls are in `TUNING`. Dev Mode offers cheats, spawns, travel, sliders, resets, clipboard export and overlays. Gallery cycles skills/Tones, monsters/affixes and boss phases. Deep links include `#zone/acre`, `#boss/regent/1`, `#vigil/3`, `#gallery/skill/knell/2`, `#gallery/boss/angelus/2`, `#attract`, `#about`; `?seed=1441` fixes the campaign seed. Tests inspect `window.__diabellum` and `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n\nKeep `data/04-about.js` accurate: it generates both About/Credits and the exit interview.\nMD'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('game/src/90-start.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"prologue:{enter(){prologuePage=0;\\\", \\\"prologue:{enter(){prologuePage=0;frontFocus=0;\\\");p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'MD'\n# Diabellum\n\nEvery soul counted. Except yours.\n\nAn original gothic action RPG built from \"'`PLAN.md` on my-3D2dge v0.89.1. The single HTML file in the parent folder plays offline: open it directly in a browser. No server, account or asset download is needed.\n\nChoose one of four parishioners. Carry Mother Quillon through three chapters, collect the iron Tongue, recast the Bell and face the Angelus. The Long Vigil offers seeded dungeons, composed Wardens, tiers, Greater Vigils and records. There are 32 skills, 96 Tones, Vows, 24 Relics, four equipment sets, gems, town services, followers and a secret field.\n\nThe campaign is a condensed complete demo. It includes its ending. Optional motion-capture clips and WebGPU lighting are omitted; the native canvas lighting remains available everywhere. All art, music, sound and gibberish voices are generated by code. Music defaults to 10%.\n\n## Controls\n\n| Action | Keyboard / mouse | Standard controller |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move | WASD, arrows, or hold click on ground | Left stick |\n| Primary / skill 2 | Click / right click, or F / G | Cross / Square |\n| Skills 3-6 | 1, 2, 3, 4 | Triangle, Circle, R1, R2 |\n| Evade | Space | Right stick flick or R3 |\n| Potion / interact | Q / E | L1 / L2 |\n| Town portal | T | D-pad up |\n| Map / bag / skills | M or Tab / I or C / K | D-pad down / left / right |\n| Journal / pause | J / Esc | Create / Options |\n\nHold Shift to stand and attack. Hold Interact to revive an ally or strike the final bell. Consecrate unknown items in the bag, then equip them. L1/R1 or bracket keys change panel tabs; arrows, Enter, Escape, hover and clicks navigate the same screens. Settings includes Xbox glyphs. Touch-only devices show a controller/keyboard notice and can watch the attract reel.\n\nA second controller joins with Options, up to four players sharing one screen. In an AI Hub session the game opens directly into a shared-world Vigil for 1-4 networked players. All network communication uses the unmodified AI Hub session client.\n\n## Development\n\n`npm install` uses the pinned Playwright version and the machine'\"'s installed browsers. \"'`npm run build` produces the root HTML and `exit-interview.json`. `npm test` is the single full test command. Select a suite with `node tools/test.mjs data`, `sim`, `play`, `browser` or `hub`. `browser --matrix` adds the 14 viewport matrix; `hub --quick` omits only the extra real-minute synchronization run.\n\nDev Mode is in the pause menu. It offers live balance sliders and resets, cheats, monster/item/boss spawns, travel, overlays and a living Gallery. See `game/CONTENT.md` for adding content. Useful links are `#zone/nave`, `#boss/regent/1`, `#vigil/3`, `#gallery/skill/knell/2`, `#gallery/boss/angelus/2`, `#attract`, `#about` and `?seed=1441`.\n\n`PROGRESS.md` in the parent folder records the build and verification. The About screen and the machine-readable interview share the metadata in `game/src/data/04-about.js`.\nMD\ncat > game/CONTENT.md <<'\"'MD'\n# Content guide\n\nBuild with \"'`node tools/build.mjs`; test with `node tools/test.mjs`. The build reads `build-config.json`, joins `00-core.js`, the sorted `src/data/*.js`, then the other numbered runtime modules into one IIFE. It writes the development page, root HTML and exit interview. The root HTML runs offline.\n\n## Registries\n\n`def(kind, id, spec)` registers heroes, skills, monsters, affixes, bosses, zones, Relics and sets. Add content in `src/data/`. Simulation never reads visual rigs. Each world owns its heroes, enemies, allies, corpses, loot, hazards and effects. Separate seeded streams drive geometry, AI, dressing and loot.\n\nSkills combine shared verbs: cone, wave, bolt, chain, nova, area, lob, bell, leap, charge, blink, buff, guard, summon, corpse, heal and beam. The `skill()` helper takes the hero, ID, name, verb, weapon-damage multiplier, range, radius, cost, cooldown, native animation and three Tones. Tone modifiers include damage, range, radius, cost and cooldown multipliers; element, stun, slow, burn, pull, pool, triple, chain, pierce, leech and Ringing. Add the ID to its hero'\"'s list. Tests cast every skill and Tone.\n\n\"'```js\nskill('\"'cantor','quietAsh','Quiet Ash','wave',2.1,130,20,20,3,'cast',[\n  ['Wide','A wider verse.',{radiusMul:1.5}],\n  ['Cold','The ash chills.',{element:'frost',slow:1}],\n  ['Cinder','The ash remembers fire.',{element:'fire',burn:1}]\n]);\n\"'```\n\nA monster supplies its body, AI kind, movement, health/damage multipliers, wind-up, reach, move and death material. Native Humanoid/Blob and custom crawler, serpent, hound and moth bodies are available. Add elite patterns in `applyAffix()`. Boss data lists health thresholds and pattern IDs; `bossPattern()` is the shared library. `dealDamage()` is the only damage pipeline. Shared hazards and effect verbs carry network events, so content needs no separate per-skill networking.\n\n## World and progression\n\nA zone chooses a theme, dimensions, layout, enemy pool/count, kill requirement and interactive objects. ASCII legend: `#` stone, `H` houses, `.` floor, `~` blocked void. Add a hand-authored layout in `makeRows()`, or use its seeded hall/island/yard generators. Preserve a walkable route between the spawn, objectives and exit. Themes control ground, walls, ambient light, weather and score. Props are seeded data; native objects use `E.SHAPES`. Bells, the gate, headstone, pew and foundry wheel in `50-art.js` are original worked examples.\n\n`CAMPAIGN` orders the quest path. Each step names a zone, title, objective, line and optional speaker. `objectiveReady()` enforces requirements. New objects need an interaction in `interactNearest()` and drawing in `drawObject()`. Existing chapels, sluices, caravan, grave row, cursed chest, sermon and side crypt demonstrate events and rewards. `ATTRACT` orders the throwaway demo vignettes. The same bot drives it, followers and the campaign test.\n\nItems have eight possible slots, rarity, affixes and optional gem, Relic or set ID. A Relic declares a power and flavor; implement its modifier in `tunedSkill()`, the damage pipeline or its shared event. Town services call the same inventory operations as tests. Saves are version 2; `serializeWorld()` omits renderer/pathfinding state and `migrateSave()` upgrades older data.\n\n## Presentation and tools\n\nUse ASCII and supported engine glyphs; keep most spoken lines under 90 characters. Add barks, lore, epitaphs and taunts to their arrays. `say()` uses native Dialog portraits and deterministic gibberish profiles. `SCORES` holds original interval sequences; instruments, reverb, voices and effects are synthesized in `55-audio.js`.\n\nAll balance controls are in `TUNING`. Dev Mode offers cheats, spawns, travel, sliders, resets, clipboard export and overlays. Gallery cycles skills/Tones, monsters/affixes and boss phases. Deep links include `#zone/acre`, `#boss/regent/1`, `#vigil/3`, `#gallery/skill/knell/2`, `#gallery/boss/angelus/2`, `#attract`, `#about`; `?seed=1441` fixes the campaign seed. Tests inspect `window.__diabellum` and `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n\nKeep `data/04-about.js` accurate: it generates both About/Credits and the exit interview.\nMD'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
